hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"4201","4195 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once. We do not know this hadith to be narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah. All who narrated it from Yahya say: from Khalid ibn Madan from al-Irbad, except Shayban, who said: from Khalid from Jubayr ibn Nufayr - thus connecting it."
"4202","4196 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Umm Habib bint al-Irbad narrated to me, from her father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade approaching captive women until they deliver what is in their wombs. This hadith - similar wording has been narrated by various routes. We mentioned this hadith from al-Irbad, unless one adds a man therein or changes a wording therein, in which case it is mentioned for the addition therein."
"4203","4197 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Umm Habibah bint al-Irbad narrated to us, from al-Irbad (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade on the day of Khaybar every beast of prey with fangs, every bird with talons, the flesh of domestic donkeys, the trussed-up (target), and plunder."
"4204","4197 (m) - And with his chain, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take a tuft from the fay and say: Nothing of it is mine, not even the like of this, except what is yours - except the fifth, and it is returned among you. Return the thread and needle and what is above it. Beware misappropriation! It is shame, fire, and disgrace upon its bearer on the Day of Resurrection."
"4205","4198 - al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, from Habib ibn Ubayd, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in what he narrates: ""When I take from My servant his two precious ones (his eyes) and he cherishes them, I am not content for him with a reward for them less than Paradise."" We do not know this hadith to be narrated from al-Irbad with a better chain than this chain. Similar wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with other than this wording, so we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place."
"4206","4199 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mughirah Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Suwayd, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed I am with Allah the Seal of the Prophets, while Adam was still turned over in his clay. And I shall inform you of the interpretation of that: the supplication of my father Ibrahim, the glad tidings of Isa, and the vision of my mother in which she saw as if a light came out of her by which the palaces of al-Sham were illuminated for her, and likewise the mothers of the believers."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a connected chain better than this chain. Sa'id ibn Suwayd is a man from the people of al-Sham, there is no harm in him. As for Abu Bakr ibn Abi Maryam, our remarks about him have already been mentioned elsewhere than in this hadith."
"4207","4200 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Hani, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I sold a young camel to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then I came to him demanding payment, and I said: Pay me the price of my young camel. He said: I will only pay you in silver coins. So he paid me and paid me well. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from any other channel, and its chain is Hasan."
"4208","4201 - Ziyad ibn Yahya al-Hassani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to me, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Ala ibn Zabr narrated to us, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Abi al-Muta' narrating from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah al-Sulami (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us one morning and exhorted us with an exhortation at which hearts trembled and eyes shed tears. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, you have exhorted us with the exhortation of one bidding farewell, so enjoin upon us. He said: Upon you is fear of Allah, and hearing and obeying, even if it be an Abyssinian slave. For you will see after me severe disagreement, so upon you is my Sunnah and the Sunnah of the rightly-guided rightly-directed Caliphs after me; bite onto it with the molars. And beware of newly-invented matters, for every innovation is misguidance. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah. It has been narrated from al-Irbad through other channels, so we mentioned this route from it and restricted ourselves to this chain to the exclusion of others."
"4209","4202 - Wahb ibn Yahya ibn Zimam al-Qaysi narrated it to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yusuf, from al-Harith ibn Ziyad, from Abu Ruhm, from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, teach Mu'awiyah the Book and arithmetic, and protect him from punishment."" He said: And I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was taking sahur, and he said: ""Come to the blessed morning meal."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from al-Irbad ibn Sariyah except through this channel with this chain. The hadith of al-Irbad has two defects: one is that we do not know any notable person who narrated from al-Harith ibn Ziyad; and Yunus ibn Sayf is sound in hadith and some have narrated from him."
"4210","4203 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salim narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Awf narrated to me that Suwayd ibn Jabalah narrated to him that al-Irbad ibn Sariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to them, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws, for it is the highest part of Paradise."" This hadith, similar wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels, but we do not know it narrated from al-Irbad except through this channel with this chain."
"4211","Musnad of Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him). What Abu Juhayfah narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 4204 - Muhammad ibn Ayyub al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Abi Khalid - narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan ibn Ali resembled him."
"4212","4205 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, he said: Isma'il - meaning Ibn Abi Khalid - narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and al-Hasan ibn Ali resembled him. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed among us twelve camels; my father received a camel, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away before giving us, so we went to Abu Bakr and he gave us."
"4213","4206 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he distributed camels among us... then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Ibn Fudayl. The hadith of Ibn Fudayl from Isma'il: we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isma'il other than him."
"4214","4207 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at midday and prayed Zuhr two rak'ahs and Asr two rak'ahs, with a short spear in front of him."
"4215","4208 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Some people of Qays beset the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), wearing striped woolen cloaks with holes cut in them and carrying swords; he was displeased by their appearance, so he prayed, then entered his house, then came out and prayed and sat in his gathering, then he commanded charity or urged it, saying: ""Let a man give charity from his dinar, let a man give charity from his dirham, let a man give charity from his sa' of wheat, let a man give charity from his sa' of dates."" Then a man from the Ansar came with a purse of gold and placed it in his hand, then people followed one another until two heaps of clothes and food were seen. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beaming as if gilded. Then he said at that: ""Whoever establishes a good practice that is acted upon after him will have its reward and the like of their rewards without diminishing anything from their rewards; and whoever establishes an evil practice that is acted upon after him will bear its burden and the like of their burdens without diminishing anything from their burdens."" Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Juhayfah except with this chain. Abu Isra'il is lenient in hadith, though Sufyan al-Thawri and many others narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"4216","4209 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray Asr at al-Abtah as two rak'ahs."
"4217","4210 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr - meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw his tuft of beard white. It was said to him: Whose contemporary were you in those days? He said: I used to make arrows and feather them. This hadith has been narrated by a group from Abu Ishaq from Abu Juhayfah."
"4218","4211 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4219","4212 - Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4220","4213 - Talut ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4221","4214 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""As for me, I do not eat reclining."""
"4222","4215 - Umar ibn al-Khattab al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym al-Nakha'i narrated to us, he said: Abu Malik al-Nakha'i narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man praying with his garment hanging down, so he stopped him. This hadith: Abu Malik erred in it; the trustworthy narrators only narrate it from Ali ibn al-Aqmar from Umm Atiyyah. Abu Malik is not a memorizer; only what he alone narrates of his hadith is written down."
"4223","4216 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed at al-Batha in Makkah the traveler's prayer, two rak'ahs."
"4224","4217 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Abtah in a tent of red leather; Bilal came out to us with the leftover of his ablution water, so we stood toward him and took from his ablution water or from the leftover of his ablution water. Then Bilal gave the adhan, turning his mouth here and there, right and left."
"4225","4218 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj - meaning Ibn Artah - from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I was with the Prophet (peace be upon him) at al-Abtah, and I prayed with him Zuhr and Asr, two rak'ahs each; Bilal gave the adhan, placing his fingers in his ears, and he used to turn while giving the adhan."
"4226","4219 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, he said: I heard my father narrating that the Prophet (peace be upon him) prayed with them at al-Batha with a short spear before him: Zuhr two rak'ahs and Asr two rak'ahs, while women and donkeys passed in front of him."
"4227","4220 - al-Husayn ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Abtah when Bilal came and announced the prayer to him; he called for ablution water and performed ablution, and people began coming and taking the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wiping their faces with it. Shu'bah said: And al-Hakam narrated it to me from Abu Juhayfah."
"4228","4221 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Umays narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at al-Abtah when Bilal came and announced the prayer to him; he called for ablution water and performed ablution, and people began taking the ablution water of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wiping themselves with it. He said: Then Bilal took the short spear and walked with it with him, and the iqamah was called; he planted it before him while riders passed in front of him: women, donkeys, and camels."
"4229","4222 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, from Umar ibn Abi Za'idah, he said: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a red tent of leather. He said: And I saw Bilal bring out his ablution water; I saw people hastening to his ablution water - whoever got some of it wiped his face, otherwise he took from his companion's palm. Then he brought out a short spear and planted it, then prayed with them while animals and people passed in front of him."
"4230","4223 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Umays - whose name is Utbah ibn Abdullah - narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda. Salman came to visit Abu al-Darda and saw Umm al-Darda dressed shabbily, so he said: What is the matter with you? She said: Your brother has no need for anything of women. When Abu al-Darda came, he welcomed Salman and brought him food; Salman said to him: Eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: I swear to you that you must eat; I will not eat until you eat. So he ate with him. Then he said to him: O Abu al-Darda, your body has a right upon you, and your family has a right upon you. Give everyone who has a right his right: fast and break fast, stand in prayer and sleep, go to your wife, and give everyone who has a right his right. Then Salman stayed overnight with him until part of the night, when Abu al-Darda got up and Salman held him back; when it was near dawn he said: Get up now. So they got up and prayed, then went out to the prayer. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, Abu al-Darda stood to him and informed him of what Salman had said to him. He said: He said to him the like of what Salman had said to him. Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Juhayfah except through this channel with this chain."
"4231","4224 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Sa'igh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""This matter will remain standing until twelve take charge"" - I think he said - ""from Quraysh"" - meaning caliphs. Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know anyone who corroborated Muhammad ibn Ubayd in its narration; the memorizers only narrate it from al-A'mash from Abu Khalid al-Walibi from Jabir ibn Samurah, and that is the correct version."
"4232","4225 - Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey when he heard a caller to prayer saying: I bear witness that there is no god but Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He has renounced the rivals. He said: I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah. He said: ""He has come out of the Fire."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""You will find him a keeper of goats kept at a distance, or a keeper of dogs."" Abu Bakr said: This hadith has been narrated by others besides Abu Qutaybah, and by others besides Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan from Abu Qutaybah, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from Muslim ibn Budayl."
"4233","4226 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth and Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to me, both said: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey and they slept through it until the sun rose. He said: You are dead, so Allah returned your souls to you. Whoever sleeps through a prayer, let him pray it when he wakes; and whoever forgets, let him pray when he remembers."
"4234","4227 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, he said - and I know it only from his father - he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The world will be opened up for you until you adorn your houses as the Ka'bah is adorned."" We said: While we are upon our religion today? He said: ""While you are upon your religion today."" We said: Will we be better then, or today? He said: ""Rather, you today are better."" Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Juhayfah except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Ahmad, nor did we hear it except from Ibrahim ibn Sa'id."
"4235","4228 - Ahmad ibn Uthman and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, from al-Fadl ibn Dukayn, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Abbas, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the dowry of the prostitute, and the price of the dog."
"4236","4229 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father that he bought a slave boy who was a cupper, then ordered his cupping instruments to be broken. I said to him: Will you break them? He said: Yes; indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of blood, the price of the dog, and the earnings of the prostitute; he cursed the devourer of usury and its payer, the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed, and he cursed the maker of images."
"4237","4230 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, both said: Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ya'fur narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was delivering a sermon with Umar before him in the gathering. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The affair of my Ummah will remain standing until twelve caliphs pass - all of them from Quraysh - he said: and he lowered his voice with it - he said: so my father nudged me between my uncle's shoulders and said: O uncle, what did he say? He said: ""All of them from Quraysh."""
"4238","4231 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh al-Marwazi narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Imran ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Abi Layla - who is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman - from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that he went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Madinah to Makkah, and he continued praying two rak'ahs at a time until he returned to his house."
"4239","4232 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Ma'mul al-Warraq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Awwam narrated to us - and I think he is Sadaqah ibn Abi Sahl - from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever closes a gap in the row will be forgiven."" This hadith we heard only from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, and he was among the most excellent of people."
"4240","4233 - Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Sadaqah, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream has indeed seen me."""
"4241","4234 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Umar, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when good fortunes were mentioned. It was said: the fortune of the tribe of so-and-so is in camels, and the fortune of the tribe of so-and-so - or of so-and-so - is in sheep. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until he prayed and raised his head from bowing, saying: ""O Allah, none can withhold what You give, none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."""
"4242","4235 - Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Umar, from Abu Juhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining about his neighbor, saying: He harms me. He said: ""Place your belongings on the road"" - or ""on the side of the road."" So he placed them, and everyone who passed said: What is the matter with you? He said: My neighbor harms me; so they would supplicate against him. Then the man came and said: Take back your belongings; I will never harm you again - or as he said."
"4243","4236 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Umar ibn Musa, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I ate tharid, then came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and belched in his presence. He said: O Abu Juhayfah, the people hungriest on the Day of Resurrection will be those most satiated in this world."
"4244","4237 - al-Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Abu Juhayfah, who said: I belched in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned something similar."
"4245","4238 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna, Amr ibn Ali, and Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, they said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Ash'ath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent among us a collector with his command to take charity from our rich and place it among our poor. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah except al-Ash'ath ibn Sawwar."
"4246","4239 - Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Ru'as narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) that Banu Amir came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he saw them he said: ""Welcome."""
"4247","4240 - Hafs ibn Mahbub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Khaliq ibn Abi Mukhariq narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw Bilal, the caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), giving the adhan with his fingers placed in his ears."
"4248","Musnad of Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him). What Jabir ibn Samurah narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 4241 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named Madinah as Tabah."
"4249","4242 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"4250","4243 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over Abu al-Dahdah, then a purebred horse was brought and he rode it, making it prance. He said a hidden word, and a man from the people - while we were walking behind him - said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How many a hanging cluster of dates there is for Abu al-Dahdah in Paradise. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Simak, and I know no one who narrated it from Simak more eminent than Shu'bah, so we sufficed with the hadith of Shu'bah."
"4251","4244 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wide mouth, eyes with a reddish tinge, and lean heels. He said: I said: What is lean heels? He said: Little flesh on the heels. This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording through a better chain than this - neither from Jabir nor from others."
"4252","4245 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Seal of Prophethood on the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) like a pigeon's egg. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Jabir ibn Samurah except through the hadith of Simak, and we do not know anyone more established regarding Simak than Shu'bah."
"4253","4246 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Religion will remain standing, supported by a group of Muslims, until the Hour comes."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Jabir ibn Samurah; similar wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other channels."
"4254","4247 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There will be twelve rulers,"" then he said a word I did not hear. I said to my father: What did he say? He said: ""All of them from Quraysh."""
"4255","4248 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace be upon him) similarly."
"4256","4249 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the sermon on the pulpit standing, except that he would sit for a sitting, then stand."
"4257","4250 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: A hairy, short man with muscular arms was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought such a man - who confessed that he had committed adultery. He turned him away twice, then ordered regarding him and he was stoned. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every time we go out as raiders in the path of Allah, one of them stays behind, bleating like the bleating of a billy goat, granting one of them a heap of dates; I will not be brought any one of them except that I make an example of him. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Simak from Jabir ibn Samurah - among them Isra'il, Abu Awanah, and others. Shu'bah is the best of them in narrating it from Simak, and the most complete in narration."
"4258","4251 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man asked him: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do when he prayed Fajr? He said: He would sit in his place until the sun rose."
"4259","4252 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Before the Hour there will be impostors."" Simak said: I heard my father saying: Beware of them."
"4260","4253 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was moderate, and his sermon was moderate."
"4261","4254 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""People from my Ummah will surely conquer the white treasures of Kisra."""
"4262","4255 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed I know a stone in Makkah that used to greet me when I was sent."""
"4263","4256 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Ibrahim and Sulayman ibn Mu'adh."
"4264","4257 - al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Talhah narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak - meaning Ibn Harb - from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I prayed the first prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he went out to his family and was met by the children of the people of Madinah; he began wiping the cheek of each one. As for me, he wiped my cheek, and I felt coolness and fragrance as if it had been in a perfumer's box."
"4265","4258 - Abdullah ibn al-Harith al-Marwazi narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from Shu'bah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Uthman ibn Jabalah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it besides Shu'bah except Asbat ibn Nasr."
"4266","4259 - Mu'adh ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Sharik."
"4267","4260 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Zuhr and Asr ""Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High"" and ""Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"4268","4261 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Zuhr when the sun had declined. Abu Bakr said: This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"4269","4262 - Yusuf ibn Musa and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih informed us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not die until most of his prayer was sitting. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except al-Hasan ibn Salih."
"4270","4263 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not have the adhan called for him for the two Eids."
"4271","4264 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Bilal would never miss the time, though he would sometimes delay the iqamah a little."
"4272","4265 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Laylat al-Qadr: that it is a night of wind and rain."
"4273","4266 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik narrated to us, from his father, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan, for I have seen it then forgotten it; it is a night of rain"" - or he said - ""of rain and wind."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Sharik, and we do not know anyone who narrates it with this wording from Sharik except Abd al-Rahman ibn Sharik from his father."
"4274","4267 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""Seek Laylat al-Qadr in the last ten of Ramadan."""
"4275","4268 - Mu'adh ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would mention poetry in his presence and recite it among themselves, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes smile. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Sharik."
"4276","4269 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that some people had a mule die, and they had nothing to eat, so they came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he permitted it for them."
"4277","4270 - Abdullah ibn Ja'far al-Barmaki narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Satan appeared before me and began casting sparks of fire at me; had it not been for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, I would have seized him."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Isra'il."
"4278","4271 - al-Abbas ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Bilal would give the adhan, then wait; when he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would begin the iqamah. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Isra'il."
"4279","4272 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Saluli narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclining on a cushion on his left side. This hadith is only an excerpt from the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought Ma'iz to stone him; Isra'il added this phrase in it, so it was written because of the addition. Otherwise, the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah regarding the stoning of Ma'iz was narrated by Shu'bah, Isra'il, and Abu Awanah."
"4280","4273 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih ibn Muslim al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Nasih Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: When it was the day of Fitr, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would eat seven dates before going out; and when it was the day of sacrifice he would taste nothing until he returned. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Nasih Abu Abdullah, who is lenient in hadith; only what none other narrates is written from his hadith."
"4281","4274 - al-Abbas ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Nasih Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: ""For one of you to discipline his child is better for him than giving half a sa' in charity every day."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Simak except Nasih."
"4282","4275 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three white garments: a waist-wrap and an outer wrap - and Umar was shrouded in two garments. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it with this wording about the shrouding of the Prophet (peace be upon him) except Jabir ibn Samurah, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Nasih; our remarks about him have already been given."
"4283","4276 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Hara'i narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Nasih narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, who will carry your banner on the Day of Resurrection? He said: Whoever carries it in this world - Ali ibn Abi Talib. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Nasih."
"4284","4277 - Muhammad ibn Jawan ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said ""Amin, Amin, Amin."" When he descended he was asked about that, and he said: Jibril came to me and said: May the nose of whoever reaches Ramadan and is not forgiven be rubbed in dust - say Amin. So I said Amin. And may the nose of a man before whom you are mentioned and who does not invoke blessings upon you be rubbed in dust - say Amin. So I said Amin. And may the nose of a man who reaches his parents, or one of them, and is not forgiven - or they do not admit him into Paradise - be rubbed in dust - say Amin. So I said Amin. This or something like it. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Simak except Qays, nor anyone who narrated it from Qays except Isma'il ibn Aban."
"4285","4278 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr - meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Simak, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man killed himself with arrowheads, so the Prophet did not pray over him. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel from the hadith of Jabir ibn Samurah from him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left praying over him, in our view - and Allah knows best - as a punishment so that others would not do the like to themselves."
"4286","4279 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah - meaning Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Sa'id al-Hamdani, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""After me there will be twelve caliphs, all of them from Quraysh."" Then he returned to his house, and I said: Then what will be? He said: ""Then there will be killing and chaos."""
"4287","4280 - Abbad ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: al-Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated to us, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4288","4281 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Ibn Awn informed us, from al-Sha'bi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similar to the hadith of al-Aswad ibn Sa'id, except that I do not recall in their hadith ""then there will be chaos."" We do not know that Amir ibn Sa'd narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except this hadith, nor that al-Sha'bi narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except this hadith. Ziyad ibn Alaqah also narrated it from Jabir ibn Samurah."
"4289","4282 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Khalid ibn Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats of this foul-smelling plant - meaning garlic - let him sit in his house."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel, nor do we know it narrated with this wording from anyone besides Jabir ibn Samurah."
"4290","4283 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Khalid ibn Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Ma'iz came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have committed adultery. He turned his face away from him; then he came to him again from the direction of his face and he turned away; he came a third time and he turned away; then he came a fourth time. When he said that to him, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his companions: Go to your companion; if he is sound, stone him. He was questioned and found sound, so he was stoned. When the stones struck him he resisted them, and a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him with a camel's jawbone and struck him with it, killing him. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To the Fire. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No; he has repented a repentance that, had a whole nation repented it, it would have been accepted from them."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel, nor from anyone besides Jabir ibn Samurah; though some of these words have been narrated from Jabir with other wording."
"4291","4284 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Khalid ibn Jabir ibn Samurah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""My Ummah will remain upon the truth, triumphant; the affair of my Ummah will remain sound, and the enmity of those who oppose them will not harm them, until twelve caliphs take charge over them."" Samurah, the father of Jabir, said: ""All of them from Quraysh."" He said: Yes. We do not know anyone who narrated from Harb ibn Khalid except Bakr ibn Khidash."
"4292","4285 - Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A lone woman traveler is about to go out from Madinah to al-Hirah fearing no one."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel with this chain."
"4293","4286 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When Kisra perishes there will be no Kisra after him; when Caesar perishes there will be no Caesar after him. By the One in whose Hand is my soul, their treasures will surely be spent in the path of Allah."""
"4294","4287 - Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Ubaydah narrated to us, from his father, from al-A'mash, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: The first to shoot an arrow alongside the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he supplicated for him - was Sa'd."
"4295","4288 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah al-Suwa'i - of Suwa' of Qays - who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Three things I fear for my Ummah: seeking rain by the stars, the tyranny of the ruler, and denying the Decree."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Jabir ibn Samurah except through this channel. Muhammad ibn al-Qasim is lenient in hadith, though the scholars tolerated his hadith and narrated from him."
"4296","4289 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Will you not line up as the angels line up before their Lord?"" They said: O Messenger of Allah, how do the angels line up before their Lord? He said: ""They complete the front rows and stand close together in the row."""
"4297","4290 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. These words, we do not know anyone who narrates them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Jabir ibn Samurah, and we do not know any route from Jabir except this route."
"4298","4291 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he entered the mosque and saw them raising their hands in prayer, and said: What is with them, raising their hands as if they are the tails of wild horses? Be still in prayer."
"4299","4292 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi', from Tamim ibn Tarafah, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through the narration of Jabir ibn Samurah from him. Its meaning, in our view, is that the people were gesturing with their hands in prayer, right and left, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Be still in prayer."""
"4300","4293 - Ahmad ibn Isa al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah - or a man from the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pasture sheep, then he pastured camels with a partner of his whom Khadijah's sister had hired. When they finished the journey, something remained due to them both, so his partner kept coming to them demanding payment, saying to Muhammad: Go. He would say: ""You go, for I am shy."" Once she said to him - meaning the partner - when he came to them: Where is Muhammad, why does he not come with you? He said: I told him, but he mentioned that he is shy. He said: She mentioned that to her sister Khadijah, who said: I have never seen anyone more modest or more chaste than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It entered the heart of her sister Khadijah, so she sent to him and said: Come to my father and propose to him. He said: ""Your father is a man of much wealth, and he"" - I think he said - ""will not do it."" She said: Go, say a word, and I will take care of it for you; come to him when he is intoxicated. So he did; he went to him and he married him to her. In the morning he sat among the people and was told: You have done well; you have married Muhammad. He said: Did I do it?! They said: Yes. He got up and entered upon her, saying: People say I married Muhammad to her, but I did not do it. She said: Yes indeed; do not disgrace yourself, for Muhammad is such-and-such. She kept at him until he was pleased. Then she sent to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two ounces of silver or gold, saying: Buy a suit and give it to him, and so-and-so. He said - and I think he did it. This hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Jabir ibn Samurah, and we do not know anyone who transmitted this hadith from Jabir except Umar ibn Hafs from his father from al-A'mash from Abu Khalid from Jabir. Others besides Umar ibn Hafs narrated it from al-A'mash from Abu Khalid as mursal. Other wordings about the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) marriage to Khadijah have been narrated with different wordings; we shall mention each hadith with its wording in its place, Allah willing."
"4301","4294 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Aththam ibn Ali - as I think - narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Khalid al-Walibi, from Jabir ibn Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have been sent, I and the Hour, like these two - like this one from this one."" This hadith was narrated by Fitr from Abu Khalid from Jabir ibn Samurah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): like this one from this one, pointing with his two fingers."
"4302","Musnad of Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him). What Zayd ibn Arqam narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): 4295 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn Sa'd informed us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas that he said to Zayd ibn Arqam: Do you not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given a limb of game while in ihram, and he did not accept it? He said: Yes. We do not know that Ibn Abbas transmitted from Zayd any hadith other than this."
"4303","4296 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: Zayd ibn Arqam came, and Ibn Abbas said to him, asking him to recall: How did you inform me about the game meat that was given to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was forbidden? He said: Yes; he was given a leg - or a limb - of game meat, and he returned it, saying: We do not eat it, for we are in ihram."
"4304","4297 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Abdullah al-Shami, he said: I heard Mu'awiyah saying: al-Ansari - meaning Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) - informed me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A group of my Ummah will remain upon the truth."" He said: I hope you are them, O people of al-Sham. Abu Bakr said: We do not know that Mu'awiyah transmitted from Zayd except this hadith. As for Abu Abdullah al-Shami, I have not heard anyone name him, and we do not know anyone who narrated from him except Shu'bah."
"4305","4298 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."""
"4306","4299 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Wahb and from Zayd ibn Yuthay', both said: Ali adjured the people in al-Rahbah: whoever heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Ghadir Khumm - so six stood and testified that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of Ghadir Khumm: ""Am I not more worthy of the believers?"" They said: Yes. He said: ""Am I not more worthy of you than your own selves?"" They said: Yes. He said: O Allah, whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."
"4307","4300 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated it to us, he said: Ali ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"4308","4301 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A Jewish man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Abu al-Qasim, you claim that the people of Paradise eat and drink. He said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, a man among them will be given the strength of a hundred men in eating, drinking, intercourse, and desire. He said: One who eats and drinks will need to relieve himself? He said: ""Sweat that flows like the scent of musk; when that happens, his belly shrinks."""
"4309","4302 - He said: al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ya'la narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thumamah, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. Someone other than Abu Mu'awiyah and Ya'la said: from al-A'mash, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4310","4303 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah al-Muhallimi, from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4311","4304 - Ibrahim ibn Hani and al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us, they said: Musa ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, from Sufyan, from al-A'mash, from Thumamah ibn Uqbah, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man from the Ansar cast knots of magic for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he suffered pain from that. Two angels came to visit him, and one of them said to his companion: Do you know what is wrong with him? So-and-so the Ansari cast knots for him and threw them into such-and-such a well; if he took them out and threw them away he would be cured. They sent to the well and found the water turned green; they took them out and threw them away, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cured. Nothing appeared on his face, nor was it spoken of. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Zayd ibn Arqam except Thumamah ibn Uqbah, nor anyone who narrated it except al-A'mash from him, nor do we know that al-A'mash narrated from Thumamah except these two hadiths."
"4312","4305 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Abu Sa'd al-Azdi, he said: Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us, he said: We raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with us were some Bedouins. We would race to the water, and the Bedouins would beat us to it; a Bedouin would outrun his companions, fill the basin, place stones around it, and place the leather mat over it until his companions arrived. He said: A man from the Ansar came to a Bedouin and led his she-camel's halter to drink, but he refused to let him. He pulled out a stone and the water sank away; the Bedouin raised a stick and struck the Ansari's head with it, wounding him. He went to Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul, the chief of the hypocrites, and informed him - he was among his companions - and Abdullah ibn Ubayy became angry, saying: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse from around him - meaning the Bedouins - for they would attend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at mealtime. Abdullah said to his companions: When they disperse from Muhammad, bring Muhammad food so that he and those with him may eat. Then he said to his companions: When you return to Madinah, the mightiest among you will surely expel the humblest. Zayd said: I was riding behind my uncle, and I heard Abdullah ibn Ubayy - we were his maternal nephews - so I informed my uncle, who went and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for him; he swore and denied, so he believed him and disbelieved me. My uncle came to me and said: All you wanted was that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted his word and disbelieved you, and the Muslims disbelieved you. He said: There befell me such distress as never befell anyone. He said: While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, I nodded my head from distress; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, rubbed my ear and laughed in my face - nothing would have pleased me in exchange for it, neither kingship nor the world. Then Abu Bakr caught up with me and said: What did the Messenger of Allah say to you? I said: He said nothing to me except that he rubbed my ear and laughed in my face. He said: Rejoice. Then Umar caught up with me and said to me the like of what Abu Bakr said. In the morning, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surat al-Munafiqun."
"4313","4306 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a raid when Abdullah ibn Ubayy said: If we return to Madinah, the mightiest will surely expel the humblest from it. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; my people said to me: What did you want with this? I went back and slept distressed and grieved; Abdullah ibn Ubayy came and swore, so I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Allah has confirmed you as truthful. And Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed: ""They are the ones who say: Do not spend on those with the Messenger of Allah until they disperse; and to Allah belong the treasuries of the heavens and the earth, but the hypocrites do not understand."" These words, we do not know anyone who narrates them except Zayd ibn Arqam. We do not know that Muhammad ibn Ka'b transmitted from Zayd any hadith other than this, nor that Abu Sa'd transmitted from Zayd any hadith other than this."
"4314","4307 - Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman and Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Shall I not teach you what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us? O Allah, I seek refuge in You from incapacity and laziness, miserliness and cowardice, old age and the punishment of the grave. O Allah, grant our souls their piety; You are the best to purify them; You are their Guardian and Master. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from a heart that does not humble itself, a soul that is never satiated, knowledge that does not benefit, and a supplication that is not answered."
"4315","4308 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who combined Abu Uthman and Abdullah ibn al-Harith except Mu'awiyah from Asim."
"4316","4309 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children's children of the Ansar."""
"4317","4310 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Nadr ibn Anas that Anas ibn Malik wrote to him: Zayd ibn Arqam wrote that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children's children of the Ansar."""
"4318","4311 - Muhammad ibn Ya'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah - from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Zayd more trustworthy than Shu'bah; others besides one followed him in its narration, so we sufficed with Shu'bah. Ma'mar differed from him, saying: from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from Anas."
"4319","4312 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""These privies are attended, so when one of you comes to the place of relieving himself, let him say: I seek refuge in Allah from the male and female devils."""
"4320","4313 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. This hadith: they differed in its chain from Qatadah. Shu'bah said: from Qatadah from al-Nadr from Zayd. Ma'mar said: from Qatadah from al-Nadr ibn Anas from his father. Ibn Abi Arubah said: from Qatadah from al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani from Zayd. Husam ibn Misakk said: from Qatadah from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4321","4314 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi Arubah - narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"4322","4315 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he passed by the mosque of Quba and found them praying after the sun had risen, and said: The prayer of the oft-returning; they used to pray it when the young camels felt the heat of the sun."
"4323","4316 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that he saw people praying Duha in the mosque of Quba, and said: Do they not know that prayer at other than this hour is better? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of the oft-returning is when the young camels feel the heat. This hadith with this wording, we do not know anyone who narrates it except Zayd ibn Arqam, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Zayd except al-Qasim ibn Awf al-Shaybani."
"4324","4317 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the nephew of Muhammad ibn Sawa, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sawa narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When a man calls his wife, let her answer, even if she is on the back of a camel saddle."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Zayd ibn Arqam, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'id from Qatadah except Muhammad ibn Sawa."
"4325","4318 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani - who is Ibn Awf - from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh ibn Jabal to al-Sham. When Mu'adh returned he said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw the People of the Book prostrating to their bishops and patricians - shall we not prostrate to you? He said: No; had I been commanding anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would have commanded the wife to prostrate to her husband."
"4326","4319 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah - meaning Ibn Abdullah - narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim al-Shaybani, from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly. This hadith has been disputed regarding al-Qasim al-Shaybani: Ayyub said: from al-Qasim ibn Abi Awfa. Qatadah said: from al-Qasim from Zayd ibn Arqam. Hisham said: from al-Qasim al-Shaybani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla from Mu'adh. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Abu Arubah except Sadaqah, and Sadaqah is not strong in hadith, though the scholars have written his hadith."
"4327","4320 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr - from al-Suddi, from Subayh the freedman of Umm Salamah, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said to Ali, Fatimah, al-Hasan, and al-Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them): I am at war with whoever wages war against you, and at peace with whoever makes peace with you. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Zayd ibn Arqam, and we do not know any route from Zayd except this route. Subayh, the freedman of Umm Salamah: we do not know anyone who narrated from him except al-Suddi."
"4328","4321 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam used to pray over our dead, saying takbir four times; one day he said it five times, so we asked him about that. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said takbir five times."
"4329","4322 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Amr al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, who said: I prayed behind Zayd ibn Arqam over a funeral and he said takbir five times. Ibn Abi Layla said to him: Did you err? He said: No; I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a funeral and he said takbir five times."
"4330","4323 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Layth from al-Muraqqa', from Zayd ibn Arqam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly."
"4331","4324 - Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Masruq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We said to him: Narrate to us. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and alighted in a valley between Makkah and Madinah, then addressed us, saying: I am only a human; I am about to be called and I shall answer. Lo, I am leaving among you the two weighty things: one of them is the Book of Allah, and my Household - he said it three times. So we said: Who are his Household - his wives? He said: Do you not see that a woman is with a man for a time, then returns to her father and her people? His Household are his family and his kin who were forbidden charity after him: the family of Abbas, the family of Ali, the family of Ja'far, and the family of Aqil. I do not know that Sa'id ibn Masruq transmitted from Yazid ibn Hayyan from Zayd ibn Arqam any hadith other than this; most of my supposition is that Humayd ibn Mas'adah narrated it to us."
"4332","4325 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydullah al-Nakha'i, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Indeed I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the Book of Allah and my Household; they will never separate until they come to me at the Basin."""
"4333","4326 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Ali ibn Rabi'ah, who said: I met Zayd ibn Arqam while he was entering upon al-Mukhtar and I was coming out from him, and I said: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed I am leaving among you the two weighty things? He said: Yes. We do not know that Muslim ibn Subayh narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam except this hadith, nor that Ali ibn Rabi'ah narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam except this hadith."
"4334","4327 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Maymun Abu Abdullah, who said: Zayd ibn Arqam said while I was listening: We alighted with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a valley called the valley of Khumm; the call to prayer was made and he prayed it at midday. Then he addressed us, and shade was made for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a garment on a thorn tree against the sun. He said: Do you not know - or do you not testify - that I am worthier of every believer than his own self? They said: Yes. He said: ""Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master. O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him, and oppose whoever opposes him."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mughirah except Abu Awanah."
"4335","4328 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, he said: I heard Maymun Abu Abdullah saying: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam saying: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded treatment for pleurisy with Indian aloeswood and oil. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4336","4329 - al-Fadl ibn Sahl and Zurayq ibn al-Sakht narrated it to us, both said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maymun - from his father, who said: I asked Zayd ibn Arqam: What was the name of the mother of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Aminah bint Wahb. Maymun Abu Abdullah narrated hadiths from Zayd."
"4337","4330 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr ibn Dinar and Amir ibn Mus'ab informed me that they heard Abu al-Minhal saying: I asked al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with them both) about currency exchange. They said: We were traders in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about exchange, and he said: Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm; whatever is deferred is not proper."
"4338","4331 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Hasan ibn Muslim, from Abu al-Minhal, who said: I heard al-Bara and Zayd ibn Arqam narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whatever is hand to hand, there is no harm; whatever is deferred is not proper."" We do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths except Ibn Jurayj."
"4339","4332 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not trim his mustache is not of us."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Zayd ibn Arqam, and we do not know any chain for it except this chain."
"4340","4333 - al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Suhayb narrated to us, from Habib ibn Yasar, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: We used to recite: If the son of Adam had a valley of wealth, he would wish for a second to it; and nothing fills the self of the son of Adam except dust."
"4341","4334 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Umarah al-Ahmar narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Yazid, Abu Layla the freedman of So-and-so ibn Sa'id, and Habib ibn Yasar informed me, they said: We were sitting with Zayd ibn Arqam when a man came and sat down, saying: People have spoken much about these two men, Ali and Uthman - so inform me about them. He said: I shall only narrate to you what I witnessed and my heart retained: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and faced us, praised Allah and extolled Him as He deserves, then said: Do you not know that I am worthier of the believers than their own selves? He repeated it to us three times, each time we said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah - while Ali was silent. He said: Stand, O Ali. He took his upper arm - or both his arms - and raised it - or raised them - saying: ""Whomever I am his master, Ali is his master."""
"4342","4335 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: Ubaydullah ibn Ziyad sent for me, so I went to him. He said: What are these reports reaching us from you, that you narrate them and transmit them from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which we do not hear in the Book of Allah? You narrate that he has a Basin in Paradise. I said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated it to us, and we retained it. He said: You have lied; you have grown old and senile. Zayd said: Yet I heard it and my heart retained it from him, while he was saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"4343","4336 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, he said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Hayyan, who said: Husayn, Amr ibn Muslim - or Umar ibn Muslim - and I set out to Zayd ibn Arqam at his house. Husayn said: O Zayd, you have met good and seen much good: you saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), heard his hadith, raided with him, and prayed behind him. Narrate to us what you saw of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and witnessed from him. He said: O son of my brother, I have grown old, my time is distant, and I have forgotten some of what I used to recall from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whatever I narrate to you, accept it; whatever I do not narrate to you, do not burden me with it. Then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: As for what follows, O people: I am only a human; the messenger of my Lord is about to come to me and I shall answer. I am leaving among you the two weighty things: the first of them is the Book of Allah, in it is guidance and light - so he urged adherence to the Book of Allah and encouraged it - and my Household: I remind you of Allah regarding my Household. Husayn said: O Zayd, who are his Household - are his wives of his Household? He said: His wives are indeed of his Household, but his Household are those forbidden charity after him. It was said: Who are they? He said: The family of Abbas, the family of Ali, the family of Ja'far, and the family of Aqil; for charity is forbidden to them."
"4344","4337 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi Zur'ah, from Iyas ibn Abi Ramlah, who said: I witnessed Mu'awiyah asking Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him): Did you witness the Eid with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Jumu'ah? He said: I witnessed that with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What did he do? He said: He prayed the Eid and gave concession regarding Jumu'ah, saying: Whoever wishes to sit, let him sit."
"4345","4338 - Maymun ibn al-Asbagh al-Nasibi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Husam ibn Misakk narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Qasim ibn Rabi'ah, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""What an excellent man Bilal is; he is the chief of the martyrs, and the callers to prayer will have the longest necks on the Day of Resurrection."" This hadith, we do not know it from Zayd ibn Arqam except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Qatadah except Husam ibn Misakk, nor from Husam except Yazid ibn Harun. Husam is a man from the people of Basra; many scholars narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"4346","4339 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4347","4340 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yazid al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father, from Zayd ibn Arqam."
"4348","4341 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya and Abdullah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated it to us, both said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, he said: my father Yunus narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: I fell ill and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited me; then I recovered and met him, and he said: O Zayd, if your eye were as it is, what would you do? I said: I would be patient and seek reward. He said: If your eye were as it is and you were patient and sought reward, Paradise would be due to you. The wording in these hadiths is the wording of Abu Qutaybah. The hadith of Isra'il, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isra'il except Ubaydullah al-Hanafi."
"4349","4342 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Jabir, from Khaythamah, from Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No servant is afflicted, after the loss of his religion, with anything severer than his sight; whoever is afflicted in his sight and is patient until he meets Allah will meet Allah, Blessed and Exalted, with no reckoning upon him."" This Khaythamah is Khaythamah ibn Abi Khaythamah."
"4350","4343 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) nineteen expeditions."
"4351","Bishr ibn Mu'adh Abu Sahl al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Uwayn ibn Amr al-Qaysi informed us, he said: Abu Mus'ab al-Makki informed us, he said: I met Zayd ibn Arqam, al-Mughira ibn Shu'ba and Anas ibn Malik narrating that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), on the night he spent in the cave, Allah, blessed and exalted is He, commanded a tree and it grew in front of the cave and covered the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah, blessed and exalted is He, commanded the spider and it wove over the mouth of the cave, and Allah, mighty and glorified is He, commanded two wild doves and they settled at the mouth of the cave. The idolaters came from every clan until, when they were about forty cubits from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with their bows and sticks, a man among them stepped forward and looked and saw the two doves, so he went back and said to his companions: There is nothing in the cave; I saw two doves at the mouth of the cave, so I knew there is no one in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard his words and knew that Allah, blessed and exalted is He, had warded them off from him by means of them, so he prayed for blessing upon them and prescribed their recompense (i.e. penalty for harming them), and they took up in the sanctuary of Allah breeding. I think he said: So the origin of every dove in the sanctuary is from their offspring. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Uwayn ibn Amr, and he is a man of Basra, well known; and as for Abu Mus'ab, we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from him except Uwayn ibn Amr. And Umayr and Riyah were two brothers."
"4352","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Kamil ibn al-Ala informed us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Yahya ibn Ja'da, from Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah never sent any prophet but he lived half the lifespan of the prophet who came before him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Zayd ibn Arqam except through this channel with this chain."
"4353","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Amr ibn Murra, who said: I heard Abu Hamza narrating from Zayd ibn Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: You are one part of a hundred thousand parts of those who will come to the Pond. And they on that day were between seven hundred and eight hundred. And the name of Abu Hamza is Talha, the freedman of Qaraza."
"4354","The Musnad of al-Jarud ibn al-Mu'alla, may Allah be pleased with him. What al-Jarud ibn al-Mu'alla narrated, ascribed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala Yazid ibn Abd Allah, from Mutarrif ibn Abd Allah, who said: Abu Muslim informed us, from al-Jarud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on one of his journeys while mounts were few, and the people discussed mounts among themselves. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you say about a stray animal? He said: When you see a stray animal or a lost item, announce it, and do not conceal it and do not alter it; and I saw it in another place: announce it and do not conceal it and do not hide it; if its owner is recognized, well and good, otherwise it is the property of Allah, He gives it to whom He wills."
"4355","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Hilal ibn Hiqq informed us, from al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Ala, from Mutarrif, from Abu Muslim, from al-Jarud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"4356","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, informed us, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Ala, from Abu Muslim, from al-Jarud, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The lost stray property of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"4357","Bishr ibn Adam narrated it to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal informed us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, he said: Hafs ibn Khalid narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Qamus Zayd ibn Ali narrated to me, he said: al-Jarud, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The lost stray property of a Muslim is the burning of the Fire."
"4358","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, from Sa'id, from Qatada, from Abu Muslim, and he is known as Abu Muslim al-Jadhmi, from al-Jarud, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking while standing. The end of the thirty-fifth, and praise be to Allah."
"4359","The Musnad of Burayda ibn al-Husayb, may Allah be pleased with him. The hadith of Burayda ibn Husayb. Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyya informed us, from al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Burayda narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me with Ali ibn Abi Talib, and I saw harshness from him. When I came, I complained of him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he raised his head and said: O Burayda, of whomever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla."
"4360","And Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Kufi narrated it to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Abu Maryam informed us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Burayda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know Ibn Abbas ascribed from Buraydah except this hadith."
"4361","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, he said: al-A'mash informed us, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us in an expedition and put Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, in command over us. When we came, he said: How did you find your companion? He said: So either I complained of him or someone else complained of him. He said: So I raised my head, and I was a man who bowed his head much, and behold, the face of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had turned red, and he was saying: Of whomever I am his wali, Ali is his wali. So I said: I will never displease you concerning him ever again."
"4362","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed a commander, or put a commander in charge of an expedition or an army, he commanded him and enjoined upon him, concerning his own self, the fear of Allah, and good toward those Muslims with him, then he said: Fight in the name of Allah and in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah. Fight, and do not steal from the spoils, nor betray, nor mutilate, nor kill a child. And when you meet your enemy among the idolaters, call them to one of three traits or qualities; whichever of them they respond to, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them. Call them to Islam; if they respond, accept it from them and restrain yourself from them. Then call them to migrate from their abode to the abode of the Emigrants, and inform them that if they do that, they shall have what the Emigrants have and upon them shall be what is upon the Emigrants. If they refuse to leave their abode, inform them that they shall be like the Bedouin Muslims: the ruling of Allah that applies to the Muslims shall apply to them, but they shall have no share in the fay nor in the spoils. If they refuse, ask them for the jizya; if they comply, accept it from them and leave them alone. If they refuse, fight them. And when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to grant them the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, do not grant them the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger; rather grant them your own covenant and the covenant of your father and the covenants of your companions. For if you break your covenants and the covenants of your companions, that is lighter than breaking the covenant of Allah and the covenant of His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And when you besiege the people of a fortress and they want you to bring them down upon the judgment of Allah, do not bring them down upon the judgment of Allah; rather bring them down upon your judgment, for you do not know whether you will hit the judgment of Allah concerning them or not. Abd al-Rahman said: This is, in my view."
"4363","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Ahmad informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put a commander in charge of an expedition or sent an army... and he mentioned similar to the hadith of Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, and he added in it: Alqama ibn Marthad said: So I mentioned that to Muqatil ibn Hayyan, and he said: Muslim ibn al-Haysam narrated to me, from al-Nu'man ibn Muqarrin, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith was narrated by Shu'ba from Alqama ibn Marthad from Ibn Burayda, mursal, thus; Ibn Abi Adi narrated it, and Abd al-Samad narrated it from Shu'ba, from Alqama, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4364","And al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated it, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Shu'ba, from Alqama, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to the hadith of Abd al-Rahman. Abd al-Rahman ibn Isa narrated it to us with it, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih informed us, from al-Layth ibn Sa'd, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Shu'ba, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4365","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us; Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever plays nardashir, it is as if he dipped his hand in the flesh and blood of a pig. And these words, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from the narration of Burayda, and we do not know for it from Burayda any channel except this channel."
"4366","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer, then a Bedouin stood up and said: Who called out for the red camel? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May you not find it."
"4367","And Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated it to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"4368","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated it to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Hisham informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of Paradise are a hundred and twenty rows; my community is eighty rows of them."
"4369","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Dirar ibn Amr, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nations on the Day of Resurrection are a hundred and twenty rows; my community is eighty rows of them."
"4370","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, both said: Mu'ammal informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr. And this hadith is only narrated from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ata; and we do not know anyone who said: from Alqama, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, except Mu'ammal from al-Thawri."
"4371","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution for every prayer, until the day of the conquest of Mecca; for he prayed the prayers with a single ablution and wiped over his leather socks. Umar said to him: You have done today something you never did. He said: I did it deliberately, O Umar."
"4372","And Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated it to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"4373","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, both said: Harami ibn Umara ibn Abi Hafsa informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The sanctity of the wives of the fighters against those who stay behind is like the sanctity of their mothers. And there is no one among those who stay behind who remains behind in the family of one of the fighters except that it will be said to him on the Day of Resurrection: Take from his good deeds whatever you wish. He said: So what do you think? And this hadith was narrated by al-Thawri and others from Alqama, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'ba except Harami."
"4374","Abda narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam informed us, he said: Mis'ar informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording ends here in the source.]"
"4375","Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, both said: Harami ibn Umara informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he passed by the graves, used to say: Peace be upon the abodes of a believing people, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you. May the Mighty Allah forgive us and you, and have mercy on us and you."
"4376","And Abda narrated it to us, he said: Mu'awiya ibn Hisham informed us, from Sufyan, from Alqama, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And the hadith of Shu'ba from Alqama, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'ba except Harami ibn Umara."
"4377","Al-Hasan ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the times of prayer. So he prayed Zuhr when the sun declined, and prayed Asr when the shadow of everything became equal to it, and prayed Maghrib when the sun set, and prayed Isha when the twilight disappeared, and prayed Fajr when dawn broke. Then he prayed Zuhr when the shadow of everything became equal to it, and Asr when the shadow of everything became twice it, and Maghrib when the sun set at its time of yesterday, and Isha after it had grown dark, and prayed Fajr when it had become bright. Then he said: Where is the questioner about the times of prayer? Between these two is the time."
"4378","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, he said: Harami informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the times of prayer. And Bundar had nothing of his wording except this. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Shu'ba except Harami, nor did anyone narrate it from al-Thawri except Ishaq ibn Yusuf."
"4379","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution washing once each."
"4380","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Faryabi informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves; permission has been given to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to visit the grave of his mother, so visit it as it suits you, for it reminds of the Hereafter. And I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrifices, that you eat it beyond three days; I only intended by that that those of means make room for those without means, so eat of it as it suits you. And I had forbidden you from vessels, though vessels neither permit nor forbid anything; and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"4381","Abd al-Rahman ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abu Zuhayr al-Marwazi informed us, he said: Ibn al-Ashja'i informed us, from his father, from al-Thawri, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is nothing but it is more obedient to Allah, blessed and exalted is He, than the son of Adam. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Zuhayr from Ibn al-Ashja'i from his father from al-Thawri. And the hadith of Ali ibn Qadim, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri except Ali ibn Qadim, and he was not followed in it."
"4382","And Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the grave of his mother amid a thousand masked men. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Yahya ibn al-Yaman, from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from his father; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya connected (mawsul) among those whose hadith is used as proof."
"4383","And it is only narrated from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, mursal. And Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman informed us, from Sufyan, from Alqama ibn Marthad, mursal."
"4384","Abda ibn Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: al-Mas'udi informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I love horses; is there any horse in Paradise? He said: If Allah admits you into Paradise, whenever you wish to ride a horse of red ruby that flies with you in Paradise wherever you wish, you shall ride it. He said: And another came and said: O Messenger of Allah, are there camels in Paradise? He said: If Allah admits you into Paradise, you shall have therein whatever your soul desires and your eye delights in. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Alqama, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, except al-Mas'udi; and others besides al-Mas'udi narrated it from Alqama ibn Marthad from Ibn Sabit."
"4385","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan informed us, from Layth, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The people of the covenant keep whatever of their properties, lands, offspring, slaves and livestock they embraced Islam upon; upon them concerning it is nothing except the charity (zakat). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Burayda, and we do not know for it any channel except this channel from Burayda."
"4386","Abu Ghassan Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Sufyan informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, from Muhammad ibn Juhada, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Superstitious omens were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Whoever is afflicted by any of that, and it is unavoidable - and the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it is unavoidable was dearer to us than such-and-such - let him say: O Allah, there is no omen but Your omen, and no good but Your good, and no god but You. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Burayda, and we do not know for it any channel except this channel; and we do not know Muhammad ibn Juhada ascribed from Alqama ibn Marthad except this hadith."
"4387","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Sufyan informed us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far informed us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man was in tawaf carrying his mother, circling with her, and he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Have I fulfilled her right? He said: No, not even for a single groan, or as he said. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel."
"4388","Abd Allah ibn al-Waddah al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Yaman informed us, from A'idh ibn Nusayr, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he mentioned the Pond and said: You shall see in it pitchers numbering the stars of the sky. And in it is other speech besides this, and it is a strange hadith."
"4389","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call the hypocrite master; for if you do, you anger your Lord, blessed and exalted is He."
"4390","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you send a messenger to me, send one handsome of face and handsome of name. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except Qatada."
"4391","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: al-Muthanna ibn Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The death of the believer is with sweat on the brow."
"4392","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Ya'qub al-Duba'i informed us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know Kahmas ascribed from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except this hadith, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Kahmas except Yusuf ibn Ya'qub."
"4393","Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Bayan informed us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording ends here in the source.]"
"4394","And Bishr ibn Adam narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: Salih ibn Hayyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The black seed is a cure for every disease except death."
"4395","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl and al-Hasan ibn Yunus narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Mansur informed us, he said: Isra'il informed us, from Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant shall never be tested with anything harder upon him than associating partners with Allah; and a servant shall never be tested with anything after associating partners with Allah harder upon him than the loss of his sight; and a servant shall never be tested with the loss of his sight and remain patient but he shall be forgiven. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Isra'il except Ishaq ibn Mansur."
"4396","Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr, said Abu Mas'ud, al-Jurayri informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: How do you say, O Hamza, when you go to your bed? He said: I say such-and-such. He said: And how do you say, you, O Ali? He said: I say such-and-such, I think he said: When you go to your bed, say: Praise be to Allah who favored me and bestowed; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, Lord of everything and God of everything; I seek refuge in You from the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Jurayri except Yahya ibn Kathir, and he was not a memorizer."
"4397","I heard Amr ibn Ali saying: I heard Yahya ibn Kathir saying: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one day with his companions, and when he finished, he said: How did you find my prayer? They said: How excellently you prayed. He said: I forgot such-and-such verse; among the excellence of a man's prayer is that he retains the recitation of the imam. Amr ibn Ali said: So I did not narrate it, and I did not narrate it from this man, and I did not write it down. Abu Bakr said: And I did not write it down; I only memorized it from Amr ibn Ali. And we do not know these words narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel."
"4398","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us; Ishaq ibn Shahin al-Wasiti informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: Ajlah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent two armies to Yemen and put Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, in command of one of them and Khalid ibn al-Walid over the other, and said to them: When you agree, Ali is over the people; and if you separate, each one is over his companions. So we met and the Muslims triumphed over the idolaters; we killed the fighters and took the offspring captive. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, chose for himself a woman from the captives. Khalid ibn al-Walid wrote with me to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and Khalid ordered me to speak ill of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. When the letter was read to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I spoke ill of Ali, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: So I saw anger in his face, and I said: O Prophet of Allah, you sent me with a man and ordered me to obey him, so I did what I was sent with. He said: O Burayda, do not fall upon Ali, for he is from me and I am from him. And we do not know anyone who narrated these words from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, with a chain better than this chain."
"4399","And al-Jurayri narrated it, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father. And Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated it to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4400","Yahya ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah informed us, from Dalham ibn Salih, from Jubayr ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Negus gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two black plain leather socks, and he wore them and used to wipe over them."
"4401","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Sharik, from Abu Rabi'a al-Iyadi, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, loves four and commanded me to love them. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: Ali is among them, and Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, and Salman al-Farisi, and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad al-Kindi."
"4402","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Abu Rabi'a, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: You have the first glance, so do not follow the glance with another glance. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Abu Rabi'a, nor do we know anyone who narrated from Abu Rabi'a except Sharik and al-Hasan ibn Salih."
"4403","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Yahya ibn Zabban al-Anazi informed us, he said: Mindal ibn Ali informed us, or Hibban, from Abd Allah ibn Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, who said: Some people came to my father and said: Leave us alone. So he said to my mother and those of the household around him: Rise. So they rose, and I remained. They said: Leave us alone. He said: He is only my son. They said: Who was the dearest of people to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4404","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih informed us, he said: Khalid ibn Ubayd Abu Isam informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Burayda informed me, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took me to a place in the desert, a salty land, around it water, near Mecca, and said: From this place the Beast shall emerge; it is a spot a handspan in a forearm's length. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except with this chain through this channel."
"4405","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mutawakkil and Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, and the wording is Ya'qub's, both said: Abu Tumayla informed us, he said: al-Zubayr ibn Junada informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night he was taken by night, Jibril came to the rock at Bayt al-Maqdis and placed his finger in it and pierced it, and tied the Buraq with it. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zubayr ibn Junada except Abu Tumayla, nor do we know this hadith narrated except from Burayda."
"4406","Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There shall come a people small of eyes, broad of faces, as if their faces are hammered shields; they shall drive the people of Islam to the places where wormwood grows, as if I am looking at them having tied their horses to the pillars of the mosque. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? He said: They are the Turks."
"4407","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, he said: Ibn Burayda informed us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A hundred years shall not pass while an eye blinks."
"4408","Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Awn informed us, from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it reached him that a woman of the Ansar had a son who died and she grieved over him. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up, with his companions with him. When he reached the door of the woman, it was said to the woman: The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wishes to come in to her to console her. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered and said: It has reached me that you despaired over your son. She said: O Prophet of Allah, why should I not despair when I am a woman whose children do not live? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truly childless woman is she whose child lives; no Muslim woman or Muslim man loses a soul - or he said - three of his children and anticipates reward for them but Paradise becomes obligatory for him. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who was on the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: By my father and mother, and two? The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And two."
"4409","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He said: I was sent, and the Hour, like these two, and he joined his two fingers, the index and the middle."
"4410","Amr ibn Musa al-Sami narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal al-Rasibi Muhammad ibn Sulaym informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever composes obscene poetry in Islam, his tongue is wasted. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Burayda."
"4411","Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Adami narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Mashat informed us, he said: Abu Hilal informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hilal except Zakariyya ibn Yahya."
"4412","Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears that he is free of Islam, if he is lying, he is as he said; and if he is truthful, he shall never return to Islam sound. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Burayda from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor do we know for it a channel from Burayda except al-Husayn ibn Waqid from Ibn Burayda from his father."
"4413","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon when al-Hasan and al-Husayn, may Allah be pleased with them both, came forward wearing two shirts, stumbling and rising. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) descended from the pulpit, took them and placed them before him, then said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: Your wealth and your children are but a trial. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Burayda, nor do we know for it any channel except this channel."
"4414","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, that when Salman al-Farisi came to Medina, he brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a table with fresh dates upon it. He said to him: What is this, O Salman? He said: Charity I gave in charity upon you and your companions. He said: We do not eat charity. Then when it was the next day he came with the like of it and placed it before him. He said: O Salman, what is this? He said: A gift. So he said: Eat, and he ate, and he looked at the seal on his back. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought him for such-and-such dirhams from some Jews, on condition that he plant for them such-and-such date palms and work until they bear fruit. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) planted the palms except one palm which someone else planted, and the palms bore fruit that year except the palm which someone else planted. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who planted it? They said: So-and-so. So he uprooted it and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) planted it, and it bore fruit that year. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Burayda from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4415","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lineage of the people of this world in this world is wealth."
"4416","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five none knows but Allah, blessed and exalted is He: Indeed, Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain, and knows what is in the wombs; and no soul knows what it will earn tomorrow, and no soul knows in what land it will die; indeed, Allah is Knowing, Aware."
"4417","Abda ibn Abd Allah and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front, and a man is most entitled to the front of his horse."
"4418","Abda ibn Abd Allah and Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, both said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Maghrib and Isha: By the night when it covers, and: By the morning brightness; and he used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming."
"4419","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal led his companions in the Isha prayer and recited: The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split. A man prayed and left. Mu'adh spoke harsh words, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining that he had been working in his date palms. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite in them: By the sun and its brightness, and the like of surahs."
"4420","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between us and them is the abandonment of prayer; whoever abandons it has disbelieved."
"4421","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, may Allah be pleased with him: that a black woman vowed: If Allah, blessed and exalted is He, brings His Messenger back safe on a campaign he fought, she would beat the tambourine over his head. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and she came and said: O Messenger of Allah, I had vowed: If Allah, blessed and exalted is He, returns you safe, that I beat the tambourine in your presence. He said: If you vowed it, do it, otherwise not. He said: So she beat it. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, entered while she was beating, and others entered while she was beating. When Umar came, she threw down the tambourine. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am here, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him; I think the devil flees from you, O Umar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Burayda, nor do we know for it any channel from Burayda except this channel."
"4422","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw in it a palace. I said: Whose is this? They said: For an Arab man. I said: I am an Arab. I said: Whose is this palace? They said: For a man of the community of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I said: I am Muhammad. Then I said: Whose is this palace? They said: For Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him. Had it not been for your jealousy I would have entered it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, would I ever be jealous regarding you? And these words were partly narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various channels, but we do not know them narrated with this wording except from Burayda with this chain."
"4423","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man said on the day of Uhud: O Allah, if Muhammad is upon the truth, cause him to be swallowed up; so he was swallowed up."
"4424","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In man there are three hundred and sixty joints; upon every joint is charity. They said: O Messenger of Allah, who can bear that? He said: Phlegm he buries is charity, removing harm from the road is charity, and the two rak'as of Duha suffice for that."
"4425","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I heard a light footstep before me. I said: Who is this? It was said: Bilal. I said: By what did you precede me to Paradise? He said: I never broke ablution but I performed ablution, and I never performed ablution but I saw it due upon me to Allah, blessed and exalted is He, to pray two rak'as. He said: It is for that."
"4426","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq informed us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Waqid informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on Hira and it shook. He said: There is none upon you but a prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. And upon it were the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman and Ali, may Allah be pleased with them all."
"4427","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted is He, sends a wind at the turn of a hundred years, and it takes the soul of every believer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Burayda with this chain."
"4428","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn al-Baqara and Al Imran, for they shall come on the Day of Resurrection as if they are two clouds, or two canopies, or two flocks of birds in ranks, pleading on behalf of their companion. Learn al-Baqara, for taking it is blessing, and leaving it is regret, and the sorcerers cannot handle it. This is the wording of Bashir or similar. And the meaning of They shall come on the Day of Resurrection is that their reward shall come, as it is narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: The morsel shall come like Uhud; and he said: The shade of the believer on that day is his charity; all of this is upon its reward."
"4429","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hayyan ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Between every two calls there is a prayer, except Maghrib. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it except Burayda, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Hayyan ibn Ubayd Allah; and Hayyan is a man of Basra, well known, there is no harm in him."
"4430","Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyayna informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: al-Muqawqis the Copt gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two slave girls, two sisters; one of them Mariya, the mother of Ibrahim, son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the other the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to Hassan ibn Thabit, and she is the mother of Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit. And he gifted him a mule, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accepted that from him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Burayda, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Bashir ibn al-Muhajir. And Muhammad ibn Ziyad erred in this hadith, narrating it from Ibn Uyayna, though Ibn Uyayna has nothing from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir; rather this hadith was narrated from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir by Hatim ibn Isma'il and Dalham ibn Dahtam."
"4431","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Ubayd Allah informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Burayda informed us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are of disrespect: that a man urinate standing, or wipe his forehead before finishing his prayer, or blow in his prostration. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except Sa'id ibn Ubayd Allah; and Abd Allah ibn Dawud and Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated it from Sa'id; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah except Nasr ibn Ali."
"4432","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Dawud informed us, he said: al-Walid ibn Tha'laba informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who swears by trust, and he is not of us who alienates a wife or a slave."
"4433","And Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir informed us, from Layth, from Uthman - and Layth did not ascribe him - from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears by trust is not of us."
"4434","Bishr ibn Adam and Zayd ibn Akhzam al-Ta'i narrated to us, both said: Abu Asim informed us, he said: Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: Husayn al-Mu'allim informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whomever we employ upon work and provide him provision for it, whatever he takes beyond his provision is misappropriation. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know Husayn al-Mu'allim ascribed from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except this hadith."
"4435","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Najiya informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muslim Abu Tayba al-Khurasani informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Burayda informed us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my companions dies in a land, he is an intercessor for that land, and a leader for them on the Day of Resurrection - or he said - an intercessor for the people of that land on the Day of Resurrection."
"4436","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muslim Abu Tayba al-Khurasani informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever of my companions dies in a land, he is an intercessor for the people of that land on the Day of Resurrection."
"4437","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumayla Yahya ibn Wadih informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muslim Abu Tayba al-Sulami informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and whenever anything remained he would load it upon me, and he named me al-Zamila (the pack-carrier)."
"4438","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Muslim informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a man entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing an iron ring. He said: Why do I sense from you the smell of idols? So he went and made it of brass. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him words concerning it. He said: O Messenger of Allah, of what shall I make it? He said: Make it of silver and do not exceed a mithqal."
"4439","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd informed us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him: The seven heavens and the seven earths and the mountains curse the old adulterer, and the private parts of adulterers harm the people of the Fire with the stench of their odor."
"4440","And Amr ibn Malik narrated it to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, from Salih ibn Hayyan, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And we do not know anyone who raised this hadith except Abu Mu'awiya."
"4441","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Subayh Abu al-Ala informed us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting in prayer: If the son of Adam had a valley of gold, he would seek a second to it; and if he were given a second, he would seek a third to it; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust; and Allah turns to whoever turns. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim from Abu al-Ala; and this is of what used to be recited, then abrogated."
"4442","Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman informed us, from Isa ibn Ubayd, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Burayda narrating from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was traveling, heard a clamor. He said: What is this noise? They said: O Prophet of Allah, some people have a drink they drink. So he sent to the people and called them, and said: Do not drink except what you have tied up - then he said - drink, and every intoxicant is forbidden."
"4443","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from Dirar Abu Sinan, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, and he is Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you from visiting graves, so visit them; and I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrifices, that you keep it beyond three days, so keep it as it suits you; and I had forbidden you from nabidh except in a waterskin, so drink in vessels, but do not drink intoxicants."
"4444","And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted vessels after having forbidden them. And we do not know Salama ibn Kuhayl narrated from Ibn Burayda, from his father, except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from Salama except Muhammad ibn Ishaq."
"4445","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami informed us, he said: Salih ibn Hayyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gravest of grave sins are associating partners with Allah, disobedience to parents, withholding surplus water, and withholding the stallion. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with the narration of Burayda from him, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Salih ibn Hayyan except Umar ibn Ali."
"4446","Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Busri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: Salih ibn Hayyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touched an idol then performed ablution. And I saw it with me in two places: in one place from Ya'la, and in one place from Muhammad; and its meaning is: he touched an idol then performed ablution means: he washed his hands."
"4447","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abd Allah Abu Ishaq informed us, he said: Uqba al-Asamm informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, make me thankful, and make me patient, and make me small in my own eyes and great in the eyes of people. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except Uqba al-Asamm; and he is a man of Basra, there is no harm in him."
"4448","Ma'mar ibn Sahl and Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Yusuf ibn Suhayb informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The people dispersed from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hunayn, and none remained with him except a man called Zayd, holding the reins of the gray mule of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah said to him: Woe to you, call the people. So Zayd called out: O people, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling you, but none came. He said: Call the Ansar. So he called out: O company of Ansar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is calling you, but none came. He said: Woe to you, single out al-Aws and al-Khazraj. So he said: O company of Aws and Khazraj, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calling you, but none came. He said: Woe to you, single out the Emigrants, for I have in their necks a pledge. He said: So Burayda narrated to me that a thousand of them came forward, having cast down their eyelids (in humility), until they came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they walked forward until Allah granted them victory. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Burayda, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except Yusuf ibn Suhayb; and Yusuf is a well-known man of Kufa."
"4449","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, both said: Ubayd Allah, meaning Ibn Musa, informed us, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman threw a stone at a woman, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged concerning her child five hundred, and forbade on that day throwing stones. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Yusuf ibn Suhayb."
"4450","Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Nu'man informed us, he said: Yusuf ibn Suhayb informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays toward a barrier, let him draw near to it, lest Satan cut off his prayer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Yusuf ibn Suhayb except Amr ibn al-Nu'man; and Amr is a man of Basra."
"4451","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Musawir al-Fadl ibn Musawir informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Maymun Abu Abd Allah, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: On the day of Khaybar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) halted before the people of Khaybar. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the banner to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and those who rose with him of the people rose. They met the people of Khaybar, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, and his companions were repelled, and he returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his companions calling him coward and he calling his companions cowards. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I shall give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and whom Allah and His Messenger love. When it was the next day, he called Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, handed it to him while he had ophthalmia, spat in his eye, gave him the banner, and the people marched with him. He came to the people of Khaybar, and behold Marhab chanting before them, saying. He and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, exchanged two blows, and Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, struck him a blow upon his head until the sword reached his molars, and the people of the camp heard the sound of his blow. The last of the people had not yet completed arriving before the first of them had conquered. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel with this chain."
"4452","Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Burayda informed us, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you but Allah, mighty and glorified is He, shall speak to him, with no veil between Him and him, nor interpreter. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Bashir ibn al-Muhajir except Abd al-Aziz ibn Aban; and Abd al-Aziz was not strong, and only what he did not narrate alone is written of his hadith."
"4453","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada informed us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim informed us, he said: Salih ibn Hayyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the horses lean, and set a time for their leaning, and said: On such-and-such day from such-and-such place; and he sent the horses that were not made lean short of that. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Salih ibn Hayyan except Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim."
"4454","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Hakim informed us, from Yusuf ibn Suhayb, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three the angels do not approach: the drunk, the one smeared with saffron, and the menstruating woman or the one in major impurity. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Burayda except through this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Yusuf ibn Suhayb except Abd Allah ibn Hakim."
"4455","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Imran informed us, he said: Aflah ibn Sa'id informed us, from Sufyan ibn Farwa, from his father, from Burayda al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came forward in his migration, he met a party of riders. He said: O Abu Bakr, ask the people who they are. They said: We are of Aslam. He said: You are safe, O Abu Bakr; ask them of which Aslam. They said: Of Banu Sahm. He said: Cast your arrow, O Abu Bakr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Burayda, nor do we know for it any channel from Burayda except this channel."
"4456","Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Sulayman informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Aws, from Burayda, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give glad tidings to those who walk in darkness to the mosques of complete light on the Day of Resurrection."
"4457","Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Awn ibn Umara informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Wasil, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man of Quraysh came forward strutting in a suit of his. When he stood over the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O Burayda, this is of those for whom Allah shall establish no weight on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Wasil. He is Wasil, the freedman of Abu Uyayna, a well-known man of Basra; and Awn ibn Umara was not a memorizer and was not followed in this hadith."
"4458","Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Junayd and Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab informed us, he said: Hibban ibn Ali informed us, he said: Salih ibn Hayyan informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Show me a sign. He said: Go to that tree and call it. So he went to it and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) calls you. So it leaned on every side of it until it uprooted its roots, then came forward until it came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah ordered it to return. So the man stood up and kissed his head, hands and feet, and embraced Islam. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Salih ibn Hayyan except Hibban ibn Ali, nor do we know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning kissing the head except this hadith."
"4459","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri informed us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man saying: O Allah, I ask You by virtue that You are Allah, there is no god but You, the One, the Eternal, who did not beget and was not begotten, and there is none like unto You; and he said: He has asked Allah by His name, by which when He is called He answers, and when asked by it He gives. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except Malik ibn Mighwal."
"4460","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab Ahwas ibn Jawwab informed us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is forbidden. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ishaq except Ammar ibn Ruzayq, nor do we know al-Zubayr ibn Adi narrated from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, except this hadith."
"4461","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn al-Wazir al-Ta'ifi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jabir informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until, when we were at Waddan or at the graves, he asked intercession for his mother, I think he said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, struck his chest and said: Do not seek forgiveness for one who died an idolater. So he returned grieving. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith with this chain except Muhammad ibn Jabir. And Alqama ibn Marthad narrated, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that they were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he came to the trunk of a wall and sat by a grave as if addressing it, then returned and said: This is the grave of my mother; I sought permission of my Lord to visit it, and He permitted me; and I sought permission of my Lord for forgiveness, and He did not permit me. So we never saw a day with more weepers than that day."
"4462","Ahmad ibn al-Wazir al-Basri narrated it to us with it, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad informed us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father. [The wording ends here in the source.]"
"4463","Abd Allah ibn Ahmad al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Adam ibn Abi Iyas informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We had forbidden you from joining dates together, so join them; for Allah has widened goodness. And this hadith, we do not know for it any channel from Burayda except this channel, nor do we know anyone who narrated it except Adam from Yazid ibn Zuray'."
"4464","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man does not give charity until he frees it from the jaws of seventy devils. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Mu'awiya from al-A'mash; and this Ibn Burayda is Sulayman ibn Burayda."
"4465","Muhammad ibn Umara al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Qadim informed us, he said: Qays informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought forgiveness for Ma'iz."
"4466","Al-Abbas ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi informed us, from his father, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Ma'iz ibn Malik came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned him away, then said: Smell his mouth; so they smelled him, then he stoned him. And we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said Smell his mouth except in the hadith of Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith."
"4467","Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Asadi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: my father informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A stone falls in Hell and does not reach its bottom for seventy autumns. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Muhammad ibn Aban, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Aban except Muhammad ibn al-Hasan."
"4468","Humayd ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, he said: Jarir informed us, from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, from Uthman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever shoots at us by night is not of us."
"4469","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban informed us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Ghamidi woman came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said she had committed adultery. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned away from her. She said: O Messenger of Allah, you wish to turn me away as you turned away Ma'iz; she is pregnant from adultery. He said: When will you give birth? So she went away. When she gave birth, she came with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), carrying him, and said: I have given birth. He said: Go until you wean him. So she went away. Then she came with him, and in his hand was a morsel of bread, and said: I have weaned him. He said: Bring me one who will sponsor him. A man stood up and said: I shall sponsor him. The companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began to marvel at the man, saying: He need not have sponsored him. So he ordered concerning her and she was stoned. Then he prayed over her. A man said: How do you pray over her when she is such? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has repented a repentance that, if divided among the people of Medina, would encompass them, or similar to this."
"4470","Abbad ibn Ahmad al-Arzami narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir al-Ju'fi, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Burayda, when it is time to open the prayer, say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no power nor strength except with Allah; there is no god but You alone, without partner; blessed is Your name and exalted is Your grandeur, and there is no god besides You; I have wronged myself, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You. And recite what is easy of the Quran. And bow, saying: Glory be to my Lord, the Mighty, three times. When you rise from bowing, say: Allah hears him who praises Him; O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heaven and filling the earth and filling whatever You will of things after. When you prostrate, say: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, three times; my face prostrated to Him who created it and split its hearing and sight; blessed is Allah, the best of creators. When you rise from the prostration, say: My Lord, forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me and provide for me; I am in need of whatever good You send down to me. When you sit in your prayer, never omit in the tashahhud: There is no god but Allah, and that I am the Messenger of Allah, and prayer upon me and upon all the prophets of Allah, and greeting upon the righteous servants of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Burayda with this chain."
"4471","Raja ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa informed us, he said: Bashir ibn al-Muhajir informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people break a covenant but killing spreads among them; and indecency never appears in a people but Allah unleashes death upon them; and no people ever withhold zakat but Allah withholds rain from them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Burayda, nor do we know for it any channel from Burayda except this channel."
"4472","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad informed us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Burayda, and he is Sulayman, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Ja'far, may Allah be pleased with him, when he came from Abyssinia: What is the most astonishing thing you saw? He said: I saw a woman carrying on her head a basket of food; a horseman passed and struck it and scattered it. She sat gathering her food, then turned and said: Woe to him when the King, blessed and exalted is He, sets His Kursi and takes for the wronged from the wrongdoer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, confirming her words: No nation is sanctified - or: how is a nation sanctified - whose weak does not take his right from its strong without faltering. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, nor do we know for it from Burayda any channel except this channel."
"4473","Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Sayrafi narrated to us, he said: Abu Yahya al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Farwa, from al-Mughira ibn Subay' al-Bajali, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that he heard him saying: I sat with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him as if grieving. A man said to him: Why do I see you as if grieving? He said: I recalled that I had forbidden you from the meat of sacrifices, that you eat it beyond three days; so eat, feed and store as it suits you. And I had forbidden you from visiting graves; whoever of you wishes to visit a grave, let him visit it. And I had forbidden you from dubba, hantam, naqir and muzaffat; so avoid every intoxicant, and drink in whatever suits you."
"4474","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Suwayd ibn Amr informed us, he said: Zuhayr informed us, from al-Walid ibn Tha'laba, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The master of seeking forgiveness is that a man say when he sits in his prayer: O Allah, You are my Lord, there is no god but You; You created me and I am Your servant; I am upon Your covenant and promise as much as I can; I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I did; I acknowledge Your favor upon me and I acknowledge my sin, so forgive me, for none forgives sins but You."
"4475","Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Aban informed us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifa informed us, from Abu Hashim, from Ibn Burayda, from his father. [The wording ends here in the source.]"
"4476","And Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Qays, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A judge who judged unjustly is in the Fire; a judge who judged without knowledge is in the Fire; and a judge with truth is in Paradise."
"4477","Al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Khidash informed us, he said: Isa ibn al-Musayyab informed us, from Atiyya al-Awfi, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man is employed over ten or more but he shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck; if he was good, his chain shall be loosened, and if he was evil, chain shall be added to his chain."
"4478","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us, he said: Husam ibn Misakk informed us, from Abd Allah, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed, some poetry is wisdom."
"4479","Raja ibn Muhammad and Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Raqashi narrated to us, both said: Malik ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Humayd al-Ru'asi informed us, he said: Abd al-Karim ibn Salit informed us, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, who said: Some people said to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Why do you not propose to Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her? So he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: What does Ali need? He said: I mentioned Fatima, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Welcome and congratulations; he did not add to them. So Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went out to that group while they were waiting for him. They said: What is behind you? He said: I do not know except that he said to me: Welcome and congratulations. They said: It suffices you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he gave you family and gave you welcome. He said: When, after a while, he married her to him, he said: O Ali, a wedding must have a feast. And Sa'd said: I have a ram, and a group of the Ansar gathered for him. When it was the night of consummation, he said: O Ali, do not do anything until you meet me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for water, performed ablution from it, then poured it over Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, then said: O Allah, bless them both and bless for them in their offspring."
"4480","The Musnad of Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him. The hadith of Wa'il ibn Hujr, and he is counted among the Medinans. Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, who said: Salama ibn Yazid al-Ju'fi asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, what if rulers rise over us who ask us their right and withhold our right; what do you command us? So he turned away from him. Then he asked him and he turned away from him. Then he asked him and he turned away from him. Then he said: Hear and obey, for upon you is only what you were burdened with, and upon them is what they were burdened with."
"4481","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, that Tariq ibn Suwayd asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about wine used as medicine. He said: It is not medicine, but it is disease."
"4482","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, both said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Simak, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do not call grapes karm; rather it is the habala (vine)."
"4483","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted him land as a grant. He said: So he sent Mu'awiya with me and said: Give it to him. He said: So I went out riding while Mu'awiya walked in midday. Mu'awiya said: Let me ride behind you. I said: You shall not be of the followers of kings. He said: Then give me your sandal. I said: Wear the shade of the she-camel. When Mu'awiya became caliph, I came to him and he seated me with him on the couch and reminded me of the hadith. So I wished I had carried him before me. And these hadiths, we do not know anyone who narrated them with these wordings except Wa'il ibn Hujr, nor do we know for them any channel from Wa'il except this channel."
"4484","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Ali informed us, he said: Abu al-Ahwas informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: A man of Hadramawt and a man of Kinda came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Hadrami said: O Messenger of Allah, this one has overpowered me over land that belonged to my father. The Kindi said: It is my land and in my possession; he has no right in it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the Hadrami: Have you proof? He said: I have no proof. He said: He swears. He said: Then he will swear, not caring about what he swears upon; he does not scruple at anything. He said: You have nothing but that. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears over the property of his brother and consumes it unjustly shall meet Allah while He is averse from him."
"4485","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when two men came to him disputing over land. One of them said: This one seized my land in the pre-Islamic period, O Messenger of Allah; and he is Imru' al-Qays, and this is Rabi'a ibn Abdan. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your proof. He said: I have no proof. He said: His oath. He said: Then he will take it away. He said: You have nothing but that. When he stood to swear, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cuts off land unjustly shall meet Allah while He is angry with him. Abu Bakr said: I think he said: Whoever is granted land unjustly by his oath."
"4486","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, from al-Hajjaj, meaning Ibn Artah, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prostrated, place his forehead and nose upon the ground."
"4487","Abd Allah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi informed us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that a woman was coerced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); so he averted the hadd from the woman and established it upon the one who assaulted her, and it was not mentioned that he assigned her a dowry. And the two hadiths of al-Hajjaj, we do not know anyone who narrated them but he from Abd al-Jabbar; nor do we know Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr ascribed from Alqama ibn Wa'il, from his father, except this hadith which we mentioned before the hadith of al-Hajjaj."
"4488","Ali ibn Sa'id al-Masruqi narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Ahwas Sallam ibn Sulaym informed us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, that he prayed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he recited the Opening of the Book, and when he said: Nor of those astray, he said: Amin, raising his voice with it."
"4489","Abda ibn Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uqba and Mu'awiya ibn Hisham informed us, from Sufyan, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I had long hair. He said: Dhubab (an evil omen / fly-like). So I went and cut it. Then I came, and he said: I did not mean you, and this is better."
"4490","Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati and Muhammad ibn Musa al-Wasiti narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Sharik informed us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed and wished to prostrate, his knees fell to the ground before his hands; and when he rose, his knees before his hands. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Yazid ibn Harun from Sharik."
"4491","Ahmad ibn Abd Allah al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sila ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Abu Hani' Ash'ath ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: Hamza Abu Umar and another man narrated to me, both said: A hadith reached us from Ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr, so we met him at Wasit in a gathering and said to him: What is a hadith that reached us from you? He said: My father narrated to me, he said: I witnessed a man, and there came with a man led in a leather strap who had killed a man. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the guardian of the slain: Do you pardon? He said: No. He said: Do you take blood money? He said: No. He said: Then you kill him. He said: Yes. He said: Then go. He said: So he went with him. When he was not far, he called him and said: Do you pardon? He said: No. He said: Do you take blood money? He said: No. He said: You kill him. He said: Yes. And he went with him, doing that repeatedly, till the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he kills him, he is like him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Wa'il ibn Hujr; and Abu Hurayra narrated similar to it with other than its wording; and Hamza Abu Umar is a man from whom Awf and Ash'ath narrated this hadith."
"4492","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal informed us, he said: Asim ibn Kulayb informed us, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I observed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when he opened the prayer, he raised his hands until he brought them to his ears and said the takbir. Then he placed his right hand upon his left. When he bowed, he raised, and raised his hands when he rose. When he sat in the second upon his left leg, he folded it beneath him, then erected the right, and placed his right hand upon his right thigh and his left hand upon his left thigh, and formed a circle with his right index finger."
"4493","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hujr informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr narrated to me, from his father, from his mother, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: News of the appearance of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us while we were in great kingdom and obedience. So I rejected it and went out desiring Allah and His Messenger. When I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he had already given them glad tidings of my coming. When I came to him and greeted him, he returned my greeting, spread his cloak for me and seated me upon it. Then he ascended his pulpit and seated me with him. He raised his hand, praised Allah and extolled Him, prayed upon the prophets, and the people gathered to him. He said to them: O people, this is Wa'il ibn Hujr; he has come to you from a far land, from Hadramawt, obedient, not coerced, desiring Allah and His Messenger and his religion, a remnant of the sons of kings. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, it is only that news of your appearance reached us while we were in great kingdom and great obedience, and I came to you desiring Allah and His Messenger and his religion. He said: You spoke the truth."
"4494","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hujr informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr informed us, from his father, from his mother, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar (exchange marriage without dowry)."
"4495","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hujr informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar ibn Wa'il ibn Hujr narrated to me, from his father, from his mother, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I witnessed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a vessel with water was brought to him. He poured it over his right three times, then dipped his right in the water and washed his left with it three times. Then he put his right in the water and scooped a handful of water and rinsed his mouth and sniffed water three times and blew it out. Then he put his palms in the vessel and raised them to his face and washed his face three times, washed the inside of his ears, put his fingers inside his ears, wiped the outside of his neck and the inside of his beard three times. Then he put his right in the water and washed his right forearm with it until past the elbow three times, then washed his left with his right until past the elbow three times. Then he wiped his head three times and the outside of his ears three times and the outside of his neck, and I think he said: and the outside of his beard three times. Then he washed with his right his right foot three times, separated between his toes, or he said: ran fingers between his toes, raised the water past the ankle, then up the shin, then did the same with the left. Then he took a handful of water, filled his hand with it, placed it upon his head until the water ran down its sides, and said: This is the completion of ablution. And I did not see him dry with a cloth. Then he rose to the mosque, entered the mihrab, meaning the place of the mihrab, arranged the people behind him and on his right and left. Then he raised his hands until they were level with the lobes of his ears, then placed his right upon his left at his chest. Then he opened the recitation and recited al-Hamd aloud. Then he finished the surah of al-Hamd, then said: Amin, till those behind him heard. Then he recited another surah. Then he raised his hands with the takbir until they were level with the lobes of his ears. Then he bowed, placing his hands upon his knees, spreading his fingers, lingering in bowing till he straightened and his back became such that if a cup of water were placed upon it, it would not spill. Then he raised his head (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with humility and said: Allah hears him who praises Him. Then he raised his hands till they were level with the lobes of his ears. Then he went down to prostration with the takbir, raising his hands till they were level with the lobes of his ears. Then he fixed his forehead on the ground till I saw his nose in the dust, arched his forearms and head, spread his left thigh and erected the right, fixing the toes of his feet, and did not linger in prostration; and he raised his head. He raised his hands with the takbir till they were level with the lobes of his ears, and sat a light sitting, placing his right palm upon his knee and part of his thigh, circling with his finger. Then he went down prostrating likewise. Then he raised his head with the takbir with his hands till they were level with the lobes of his ears, till he straightened in his standing and every bone returned to its place. Then he prayed four rak'as, doing in them what he does in this one. Then he sat a sitting in the tashahhud likewise. Then he greeted to his right till the whiteness of his left cheek was seen, and greeted to his left till the whiteness of his right cheek was seen. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Wa'il ibn Hujr with this chain."
"4496","Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Mudrik informed us, he said: Khallad, meaning Ibn Muslim al-Saffar, informed us, from Musa ibn Abi A'isha, from Asim ibn Kulayb, from his father, from Wa'il ibn Hujr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I examined the prayer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him raise his hands when he said takbir, then place one hand upon the other, then when he wanted to bow he raised his hands and said takbir, then said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, and raised; I was left uncertain whether he raised when he prostrated or not. He said: He prayed two rak'as, and when he sat for the tashahhud he spread his left foot and placed his right hand on his thigh, then clenched his fingers, then made a circle and pointed with the forefinger, and gave salam to his right and to his left. He said: And I saw him saying takbir whenever he lowered and raised."
"4497","The Musnad of Abu Barza al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him. The hadith of Abu Barza al-Aslami from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi and Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Shahid narrated to us, both said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: my father informed us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and a girl of the Ansar was upon a camel of hers; she looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) behind her while the mountain passage had become narrow for them, so she said: Hal, Hal, upon you be the curse of Allah, meaning her camel. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is the owner of this camel or mount; let no camel upon which is a curse from Allah accompany us. And these words have been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with different wordings, so we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place; we do not know it narrated from Abu Barza except through this route. The name of Abu Barza is Nadla ibn Ubayd, the name of Abu Azza is Yasar ibn Ubayd, and the name of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi is Abd al-Rahman ibn Mull."
"4498","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Kinana ibn Nu'aym, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met the enemy and Allah granted him booty, so he said: Do you miss anyone? They said: Yes, so-and-so and so-and-so. Then he said: Do you miss anyone? a second and third time. They said: No. He said: But I miss Julaybib; go and seek him among the slain. So they sought him and found him beside seven whom he had killed, then they had killed him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought the news, so he came until he stood and said: This is from me and I am from him; he killed seven; this is from me and I am from him, saying it twice. Then he carried him upon his forearms, he had no bed other than the forearms of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), until a grave was dug for him and he was buried, and he did not mention washing. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Abu Barza, and we do not know for it a route from Abu Barza except this route."
"4499","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, informed us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Sharik ibn Shihab, who said: I used to wish to meet a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to ask him about the Khawarij, so I met Abu Barza on a day of Eid among a group of his companions. I said to him: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my ear and saw him with my eye: wealth was brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he gave to those on his right and those on his left, and did not give anything to those behind him. Then a man from behind him stood and said: O Muhammad, by Allah, you have not been just toward me since today. He was a black man with closely cut hair, wearing two white garments. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became intensely angry and said: By Allah, you will not find after me a man more just toward you than me. Then he said: There will emerge at the end of time a people, as if this one is of them; they recite the Qur'an but it does not pass their throats; they pass through Islam as the arrow passes through the target; their mark is shaving; they will keep emerging until the last of them emerges with the False Messiah, the Dajjal. When you meet them, kill them; they are the worst of creation and creatures. And this hadith, similar wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through more than one route, so we mentioned each hadith with its wording in its place; we do not know anyone narrated from Sharik ibn Shihab except al-Azraq ibn Qays, and we do not know he narrated other than this hadith."
"4500","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Jamil ibn Murra, from Abu al-Wadi', from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not separated."
"4501","And Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan informed us, from Jamil ibn Murra, from Abu al-Wadi', from Abu Barza, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording."
"4502","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Aban ibn Sam'a informed us, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, teach me something I may benefit from. He said: Remove harm from the path of the Muslims. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Barza. Abu al-Wazi' is a man of Basra; Ayyub, Shaddad ibn Sa'id, Mahdi ibn Maymun and others narrated from him."
"4503","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Aslam and al-Hajjaj ibn Nusayr informed us, he said: Abu Talha, and he is Shaddad ibn Sa'id, informed us, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a Hawd, between Ayla and San'a, its width like its length; two spouts pour into it from Paradise, one of silver and the other of gold, whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, cooler than snow; in it are vessels numbering the stars of the sky; whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst until he enters Paradise. Rawh said in his hadith: And Shaddad ibn Sa'id added, from Ayyub, from Abu al-Wazi', from Abu Barza, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): They leap in the hands of the believers, meaning the vessels. We do not know Ayyub narrated from Abu al-Wazi' except this hadith, and none narrated it from Ayyub except Shaddad ibn Sa'id."
"4504","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, he said: Abu al-Wazi' informed us, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a man to a clan of the Arab clans, and they reviled him and beat him. He came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him, so he said: Had you gone to the people of Oman, they would neither have beaten you nor reviled you. And this hadith, we do not know it with this wording except from Abu Barza, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and something close to it without its wording has been narrated from Ibn Umar."
"4505","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Raja' ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Dinar informed us, from Abu Hashim, from Abu al-Aliya, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and wanted to stand, he said: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I bear witness there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you say words you did not used to say before. He said: This is an expiation for what occurs in the gathering. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Barza except through this route with this chain."
"4506","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Uthman al-Ghatafani informed us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha' informed us, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Barza, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sleeping before it and conversing after it, meaning Isha."
"4507","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, from Shu'ba, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barza, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And the hadith of Khalid al-Hadhdha', from al-Mughira ibn Abi Barza, from his father: I think Uthman ibn Uthman erred in it; the correct is: Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu al-Minhal, from Abu Barza. The name of Abu al-Minhal is Sayyar ibn Salama."
"4508","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nu'man Muhammad ibn al-Fadl informed us, he said: Sukayn ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, from Sayyar ibn Salama, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rulers are from Quraysh; I have a right over them, and they have a right over you, as long as they do three things: when mercy is sought from them they show mercy, when they judge they are just, and when they covenant they fulfill. Whoever of them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels and all people. And this hadith, we know it only from Abu Barza with this chain; Sukayn is a well-known man of Basra."
"4509","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hammad informed us, he said: Abu al-Ashhab, whose name is Ja'far ibn Hayyan, informed us, from Abu al-Hakam, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only fear for you the lusts of error in your bellies and private parts, and the misleading desires. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Barza with this chain."
"4510","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Barza, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Aslam, may Allah keep it safe, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it."
"4511","And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated it to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from al-Mughira ibn Abi Barza, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Barza except through this route, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ali ibn Zayd except Shu'ba."
"4512","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Mas'ada informed us, he said: Abd al-Salam ibn Abi Hazim informed us, who said: I saw Abu Barza, and Ibn Ziyad sent to him asking him about the Hawd. He said: One who entered with him informed me. He said: When Ibn Ziyad saw him, he said: This Muhammad of yours is short and stocky. When Abu Barza heard it, he said: I never thought I would live until I am reproached for the companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: It was said to him: You are not reproached for that. He said: And Ibn Ziyad asked him about the Hawd, so he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, I think he said: I have a Hawd; whoever denies it, may Allah not bring him to it, meaning it."
"4513","Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Abu al-Musawir, who said: I said to Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him: Whom did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stone? He said: A man of us called Ma'iz ibn Malik."
"4514","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Musayyab Sallam ibn Salm al-Wasiti informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala informed us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of people are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone raised it with a chain except Mubarak ibn Fadala, from al-Azraq, from Abu Barza; and we do not know anyone narrated it from Mubarak ibn Fadala except Sallam ibn Salm."
"4515","And Abbad ibn Ya'qub al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan informed us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad informed us, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from Abu Hilal al-Akki, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at two men at Uhud versifying poetry about Hamza, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, cast them back into trial and drive them to punishment. Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas was narrated from by Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad and others; Abu Hilal al-Akki is an unknown man."
"4516","Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: Abd al-Salam informed us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Abu Barza, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in a long hadith he mentioned, that he performed ablution and wiped over the two khuffs."
"4517","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athma informed us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amir informed us, from Muhammad of the descendants of Abu Barza, from Abu Barza al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not righteousness."
"4518","Muhammad ibn Amra al-Razi narrated to us, he said: al-Sindi ibn Abdawayh informed us, he said: Jisr ibn Ja'far informed us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, who said: I heard Abu Barza al-Aslami, may Allah be pleased with him, say: I raided with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) such-and-such campaign, until he counted eight campaigns, and we saw from him nothing but ease and lightening. Abu Bakr said: Alqama ibn Marthad only narrates from Sulayman ibn Burayda, from his father; Muharib ibn Dithar only narrates from Sulayman ibn Burayda; Muhammad ibn Juhada only narrates from Sulayman ibn Burayda; and Sulayman al-A'mash only narrates from Ibn Burayda. More than one mentioned in it from Sulayman, and some said: from Ibn Burayda without naming him, and in my view he is Sulayman; the rest of the companions of Ibn Burayda only narrate from Abd Allah ibn Burayda except one man."
"4519","The Musnad of Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him. Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him. Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib ibn Yahya al-Raqqi al-Samut informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq al-Bazzar informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Awf, from Abu Raja' al-Utaridi, from Samura ibn Jundub. And I found in my book: Abd Allah ibn al-Misbah informed us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman informed us, from Awf, from Abu Raja', from Samura; the wording is the wording of Ibn Abi Adi. He said: Part of what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say to his companions was: Has any of you seen a dream? Then whoever Allah willed would relate it to him. He said: One morning he said to us: Two visitors came to me and they roused me, and they said to me: Go, so I went with them. Al-Mu'tamir said in his hadith: Tonight two visitors came to me and said to me: Go, so I went with them. We came upon a man lying down, and another standing over him with a rock; he hurls the rock at his head and crushes his head with it, then the stone rolls away and he follows the stone and takes it, and does not return to him until his head is sound as it was, then he returns to him and does to him as he did the first time. He said: I said: Glory be to Allah, what is this? He said: They said to me: Go on, go on. He said: So I went with them and we came upon a man lying on his back, and another standing over him with an iron hook; he comes to one side of his face and tears his cheek to his nape, his nostril to his nape, and his eye to his nape, then moves to the other side and does to it as he did to the first side; he does not finish that side until the first is sound as it was, then he returns and does to him as he did the first time. He said: I said: O glory be to Allah, what is this? They said: Go on, go on. So I went and we came upon something like the structure of an oven; Awf said: I think he said: in it were noise and the voices of men and women; flames come to them from beneath them, and when the flames reach them they clamor. He said: I said: Who are these? They said to me: Go on, go on. He said: So we went and came upon a river, I thought he said: red like blood; in the river a man swimming, and on the bank of the river a man who had gathered many stones; the swimming man swims, then comes to the one who gathered the stones, who opens his mouth for him and feeds him a stone. He said: I said: What is this? They said to me: Go on, go on. He said: So we went and came upon a man of ugly appearance beside a fire of his which he kindles and circles around. He said: I said to them: What is this? They said to me: Go on, go on. So we went and came upon a grassy garden with every blossom of spring; in the midst of the garden a tall man standing, and around the man the most numerous children I had ever seen; I think he said: I said to them: What is this, or who are these? He said: They said to me: Go on, go on. So we went until we came to a great terrace, I never saw a terrace greater or more beautiful; they said to me: Ascend it. So I ascended, and we came to a city built of bricks of gold and bricks of silver; we came to the gate of the city and sought opening, and it was opened for us; we entered and were met by men, half of their creation as beautiful as you ever see, and half as ugly as you ever see. They said to them: Go and plunge into that river; there was a river running across as if its water were pure milk in whiteness, so they went and plunged in it, then returned to us with that evil gone from them, become in the best form. He said: They said to me: This is the Garden of Eden, and that is your dwelling. So my sight rose upward, and there was a palace like a white cloud. They said to me: This is your dwelling. I said: May Allah bless you, let me enter it. They said to me: As for now, no; you will enter it. I said: I have seen wonders tonight, so what is this that I saw? They said to me: We shall inform you. As for the first man you came upon whose head is crushed with stone: he is a man who takes the Qur'an and rejects it, and sleeps through the prescribed prayer. As for the man whose cheek, eye and nostril are torn to his nape: he is the man who leaves his house in the morning and tells a lie that reaches the horizons. As for the naked men and women in what is like the structure of an oven: they are the adulterers and adulteresses. As for the man swimming in the river being fed stones: he is the eater of usury. As for the ugly man at the fire: he is the keeper of Hell. As for the tall man in the garden: he is Ibrahim, peace be upon him. As for the children around him: every child who died upon the fitra. As for the people half of whom is handsome and half ugly: they are people who mixed a righteous deed with another evil one, and Allah overlooked them, blessed and exalted."
"4520","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from Abu Raja', from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prayed the morning prayer, would face us with his face, then say: Has any of you seen a dream?"
"4521","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Rayhan ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Abu Raja', from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitra; his parents make him a Jew or a Christian."
"4522","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Shu'ayb informed us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur informed us, from Abu Raja', from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, so he said: They are the servants of the people of Paradise. And this hadith which Awf narrated, a group narrated with Awf, among them Hammad ibn Mansur, who added in it over Awf: He was asked about the children of the polytheists, so he said: They are the servants of the people of Paradise; and he said: Every newborn is born upon the fitra. Abu Khalda also narrated it from Abu Raja', from Samura; Jarir ibn Hazim narrated it and added in it: He faced us with his face. Jarir did not have the length of the hadith of Awf nor of Abbad; they are longer in its narration. We do not know anyone narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Samura, and none narrated it from him except Abu Raja' al-Utaridi."
"4523","And Jamil ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Mahbub ibn al-Hasan informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Abu Raja', from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4524","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Raqashi informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman informed us, he said: Awf informed us, from Abu Raja', from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Woman was created from a rib; if you insist on straightening her you break her, and if you enjoy her you enjoy her while there is crookedness in her. Abu Bakr said: This hadith was narrated from Awf by a group, from Abu Raja'; some said: from a man, and he is Shu'ba; Shu'ba and al-Thawri narrated it from Awf, from a man, from Samura."
"4525","I heard Amr ibn Ali narrating from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan, who said: I heard Sufyan narrating from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Upon you is white of garments; let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it."
"4526","And I heard Amr ibn Ali say, he said: I heard Yahya ibn Sa'id mention it, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Among the best of your garments is white; let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it. Amr ibn Ali said: I did not write down from Yahya the hadith of Sa'id, but I memorized it from him."
"4527","He said: And Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: My father informed me, from al-Mas'udi, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit and al-Hakam ibn Utayba, from Maymun ibn Abi Shayba, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Upon you is white of garments; let your living wear it and shroud your dead in it. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except from the hadith of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib and Abu al-Muhallab; we do not know anyone who said: from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu al-Muhallab, from Samura, except Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba; others than Sa'id narrate it from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from Samura; we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Hakam except al-Mas'udi."
"4528","Al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ibn Burayda, meaning Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a woman who died in childbirth; he stood and prayed over her, praying at her middle."
"4529","And Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Thaqafi, and he is Ibn Abi Safwan, narrated it to us, he said: Abu Qutayba informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Ibn Burayda, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. We do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Samura, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Shu'ba except Abu Qutayba."
"4530","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4531","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4532","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awana informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4533","And Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated it to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ulaya informed us, from Dawud al-Ta'i, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: These beggings are scratches on the face of a man; whoever wishes may preserve his face, unless he comes to one of authority, or a matter from which he finds no escape. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Samura."
"4534","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from al-Mas'udi, from Ma'bad ibn Khalid, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4535","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah informed me, from Ma'bad, from Zayd ibn Uqba, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to recite in the two Eids: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High, and: Has there reached you the story of the Overwhelming?"
"4536","Abu Kamil and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, both said: Abu Awana informed us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What do you think of the lizard? He said: A nation was transformed, and Allah knows best. He said: Uyayna ibn Badr entered and saw a cupper cupping the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a horn, and said: You let this one at your flesh? He said: This cupping is the best of what you treat yourselves with."
"4537","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Qaza'a, and he is Suwayd ibn Hujayr, from al-Asqa' ibn al-Asla', from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4538","And Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated it to us, he said: Qaza'a ibn Suwayd ibn Hujayr informed us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Suwayd ibn Hujayr, and he is Abu Qaza'a, from al-Asqa' ibn al-Asla', from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is below the ankles of the lower garment is in the Fire. Qaza'a said: What is above the ankle of the garment is in the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route with this chain."
"4539","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra narrating from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and after dawn until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. We do not know al-Muhallab ibn Abi Sufra raised from Samura other than this hadith, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Simak except Shu'ba."
"4540","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Rabi' ibn Umayla, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name your boy Aflah, nor Najih, nor Yasar, nor Rabah; for when you say: Is he there, is so-and-so there, they say: No. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Samura with this chain. Al-Rabi' ibn Umayla is well known of Kufa, and he is the father of al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi'."
"4541","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Sufyan, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Four are the best of speech; it does not harm you with which of them you begin: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest."
"4542","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far, or Abu Mu'awiya, informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever narrates a hadith from me while he thinks it is a lie is one of the two liars. And this hadith was narrated by Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Shu'ba is more retentive than Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman. We do not know Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla narrated from Samura except this hadith."
"4543","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, both said: Affan ibn Muslim informed us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is about to fill your hands with the non-Arabs, then make them lions who do not flee; they will fight your enemies and eat your booty. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Yunus except Hammad ibn Salama."
"4544","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Ali al-Maqdisi and al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, both said: Khalid ibn Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Qurra, informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The neighbor of the house is most entitled to the house."
"4545","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abu al-Walid informed us, he said: Shu'ba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The neighbor of the house is most entitled to the house or the land. It is said of al-Hasan that he heard from Samura only one hadith; he had abandoned him out of disinterest, then his truthfulness became clear to him later, so he went to his house afterward and took this sahifa and narrated it from him. What is established as heard by him from Samura is a hadith Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Habib narrated to us, from Quraysh ibn Anas, from Habib ibn al-Shahid, who said: Muhammad ibn Sirin said to me: Ask al-Hasan from whom he heard the hadith on the aqiqa? So I asked him, and he said: From Samura."
"4546","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yahya informed us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4547","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever performs ablution on Friday, that suffices, and excellent it is; whoever bathes, bathing is better. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Samura, except Khalid ibn Yahya."
"4548","Al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had two pauses: a pause when he began the prayer, and a pause when he finished his recitation. This hadith was narrated by Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, but Imran objected to it; he said: So he wrote to Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who wrote back affirming the truthfulness of Samura."
"4549","Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'a narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Khubza informed us, he said: Yunus informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to pray at night, little or much, and to make the last of that witr."
"4550","And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us, he said: My father informed us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sa'd informed us, from Habib ibn Sulayman ibn Samura, from his father, from his grandfather Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command that each of us pray every night after the prescribed prayer, little or much, and make the last of that, I think he said, witr. Ja'far ibn Sa'd is of the progeny of Samura. The hadith of Yunus from al-Hasan, we do not know anyone narrated it from Yunus except Sallam ibn Abi Khubza; he was a man of Basra with weakness regarding qadar."
"4551","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Tamim ibn Ziyad informed us, he said: Abu Ja'far al-Razi informed us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4552","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abd Allah, informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him. Hisham added in his hadith, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, what is not in the hadith of Yunus nor in the hadith of any who narrate it from Qatada: Whoever castrates his slave, we castrate him. The hadith of Yunus from al-Hasan from Samura, we do not know anyone narrated it except Abu Ja'far al-Razi from him."
"4553","And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura ibn Jundub, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills his slave, we kill him; whoever mutilates his slave, we mutilate him. Al-Hasan used to narrate this from Samura, Qatada said; then al-Hasan later forgot, and used to give fatwa that a master is not killed for a slave."
"4554","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hand is liable for what it takes until it returns it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4555","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Every boy is pledged for his aqiqa; it is slaughtered for him on his seventh day, he is named, and his head is shaved. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it with this wording except Samura."
"4556","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sam is the father of the Arabs, Ham the father of the Abyssinians, and Japheth the father of the Romans. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Samura and Abu Hurayra; the wording of the hadith of Samura differs from the wording of Abu Hurayra."
"4557","Muhammad ibn Marzuq ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you comes upon livestock, if its owner is present let him call him; if he permits him, let him milk and drink; if there is no one in it, let him call three times; if he is answered, well, otherwise let him milk and drink but not carry away. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route with this chain."
"4558","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever encloses land with a wall, it is his. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Samura. Its meaning in our view: whoever encloses with a wall land owned by no one, it becomes his because he preceded to it."
"4559","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi informed us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura or Uqba ibn Amir, may Allah be pleased with them both, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whichever woman two guardians marry off, she belongs to the first of them; and whichever man sells a sale to two men, it belongs to the first of them."
"4560","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route."
"4561","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith and Abd al-A'la informed us, both said: Sa'id informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4562","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling an animal for an animal on credit. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route with this chain."
"4563","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Shu'ba informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two sellers have the choice as long as they have not separated."
"4564","And Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated it to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And this hadith was narrated from Qatada by a group, among them Hisham ibn Abi Abd Allah, Abu Awana and others."
"4565","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4566","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi informed us, from Hisham, meaning Ibn Abi Abd Allah, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not curse one another with the curse of Allah, nor with His anger, nor with the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Hisham."
"4567","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Rain befell us while we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out: Prayer is in the saddles. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route."
"4568","Bishr ibn Adam and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, both said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade celibacy. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Hisham, nor from Hisham except his son Mu'adh. Mu'adh had once narrated it to them from his father, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, then later narrated it to them making it from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4569","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Affan informed us, from Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Qur'an was sent down upon three letters. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Hammad ibn Salama, and we do not know this wording narrated except from Samura."
"4570","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Minhal informed us, he said: Hammad informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Qur'an was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) three presentations. He said: They think, he said: I do not know whether in this hadith or another, that our recitation is the last presentation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammad, from Qatada, except al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal; we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route."
"4571","Abd Allah ibn Mu'awiya narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salama, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever owns a relative of unmarriageable kin is free. And these three hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them from Qatada except Hammad ibn Salama."
"4572","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-A'la ibn al-Qasim informed us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to greet our imams, and that we greet one another in prayer. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Samura."
"4573","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt or her maternal aunt. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammam except Muhammad ibn Bilal and Ya'la ibn Abbad al-Kilabi; Muhammad ibn Bilal is more established than Ya'la ibn Abbad."
"4574","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Abbad informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped have broken the fast. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Hammam, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura; we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammam except Ya'la ibn Abbad. There is disagreement from al-Hasan: Yunus said: from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayra; Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib said: from al-Hasan, from Ma'qil ibn Yasar, and they said: Ma'qil ibn Sinan; Matar al-Warraq said: from al-Hasan, from more than one of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Umar ibn Ibrahim said: from Qatada, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him."
"4575","Raja' ibn Muhammad al-Saqati and al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Ruzzi narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Idris informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not dwell with the polytheists; whoever dwells with them is of them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, except Hammam, nor from Hammam except Ishaq ibn Idris. Its meaning is that he said: Do not dwell with them in their land."
"4576","Ahmad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Abbad informed us, he said: Hammam informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4577","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Quraysh ibn Anas informed us, from Ash'ath, meaning Ibn Abd al-Malik, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade cutting the strap between the two fingers. We do not know anyone narrated this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Samura; we do not know anyone narrated it from Hammam, from Qatada, except Ya'la ibn Abbad, nor from Ash'ath except Quraysh ibn Anas. Ya'la ibn Abbad narrated hadiths not corroborated; of what he narrated from Hammam of the hadiths of Samura, he was not corroborated except in a hadith we have clarified, which Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated."
"4578","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan and al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, both said: Ishaq ibn Idris informed us, he said: Suwayd ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The wording of the hadith is not present in the source.]"
"4579","And Abd al-Rahman ibn Isa ibn Sasan al-Susi and Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, both said: Abu al-Jumahir informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Matar, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he prayed for rain he said: O Allah, make in our land its adornment and its settlement. The hadith of Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura: we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Suwayd ibn Ibrahim Abu Hatim, a Basran shaykh, no harm in him. The hadith of Matar, we do not know anyone narrated it from him except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4580","Abu Kurayb narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiya informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill the aged of the polytheists and spare their young. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"4581","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us, he said: al-Hajjaj informed me, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The war cry of the Muhajirun was Abd Allah, and the war cry of the Ansar was Abd al-Rahman, meaning in war, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, except al-Hajjaj ibn Artah."
"4582","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud informed us, he said: Imran al-Qattan informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man shall not propose over the proposal of his brother, nor sell over the sale of his brother. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, except Imran al-Qattan."
"4583","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'id informed us, he said: My father informed me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: This verse was revealed: This day I have perfected for you your religion and completed upon you My favor, upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at Arafa on a Friday. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route; none narrated it from Qatada except Umar ibn Musa ibn Wajih, nor from Umar except Muhammad ibn Ishaq. Umar ibn Musa is lenient in hadith; only what he is alone in is written from his hadith."
"4584","Al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Azim and Salih ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, both said: Yunus ibn Muhammad informed us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is piety. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Sallam ibn Abi Muti', who was of the best and most intelligent of people."
"4585","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished for what is wailed over him. And this hadith, I think Umar ibn Ibrahim erred in it, transmitting it from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura; the trustworthy only transmit it from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibn Umar, from Umar; and from Qatada, from Qaza'a, from Ibn Umar, from Umar; and from Qatada, from Yahya ibn Rawba, from Ibn Umar, from Umar. We do not know anyone corroborated Umar ibn Ibrahim in his narration among the companions of Qatada, and we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route. Umar ibn Ibrahim has from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, three hadiths not corroborated; this is one of them."
"4586","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When Hawwa' became pregnant, Iblis circled her, and no child would live for her, so he said: Name him Abd al-Harith, for he will live. So she named him Abd al-Harith and he lived; that was of the inspiration and command of Satan. We do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Samura, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Umar ibn Ibrahim."
"4587","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith informed us, he said: Umar ibn Ibrahim informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man goes bankrupt and a man finds his property intact, he is more entitled to it than the creditors. And this hadith was narrated by others than Umar ibn Ibrahim, from Qatada, from al-Nadr ibn Anas, from Bashir ibn Nahik, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); that is the correct."
"4588","Ahmad ibn Uthman ibn Hakim and Muhammad ibn al-Layth narrated to us, both said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm informed us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: al-Firdaws is the hill of Paradise; when you ask Allah, blessed and exalted, ask Him for al-Firdaws. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik."
"4589","Rizq Allah ibn Musa and Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, both said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr ibn Salm informed us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Satan has kohl and a linctus; when he applies kohl to a man from his kohl, he distracts him from prayer, and when he gives him to lick of his linctus, his tongue becomes foul with evil."
"4590","And Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. And these words, we do not know anyone narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Samura and Anas; we do not know anyone narrated them from Qatada except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik and Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"4591","Abu Kurayb Muhammad ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, he said: Waki' informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The likeness of the early comer to Friday is as one offering a camel, then as one offering a cow, until he reached the chicken and the egg, or words to that effect. We do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except Sa'id ibn Bashir; Sa'id ibn Bashir was not retentive."
"4592","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting on the buttocks with knees up and squatting, and that we rise hastily in our prayer, and that a Muhajir pray behind a Bedouin. We do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Sa'id ibn Bashir from Qatada. Samura is alone in this hadith in the words: we do not rise hastily in our prayer."
"4593","And Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us not to rise hastily in our prayer. Hammad ibn Salama narrated, from Qatada, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade squatting and sitting on the buttocks in prayer."
"4594","And Harun ibn Sufyan narrated it to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ishaq informed us, and he said: Hammad ibn Salama informed us, from Qatada, from Anas. And this hadith, I think Yahya ibn Ishaq erred in it. Sa'id ibn Bashir: no hadith of his is adduced when he is alone in it. The preserved hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Salama and others, from Qatada, from Anas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, let him not spread his forearms as the dog or beast spreads. This is the hadith in our view, and Allah knows best."
"4595","Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Fadl ibn al-Muwaffaq narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best jihad is to speak the truth before a ruler, or he said: before a tyrannical ruler. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Hasan except Abu Bakr al-Hudhali. Abu Bakr is a man of Basra; the people of knowledge do not establish his hadith. Ibn Jurayj and those below him narrated from him."
"4596","Abd Allah ibn Ishaq al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Hubayra informed us, from Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali informed me, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The food of one suffices two, the food of two suffices four, and the hand of Allah, blessed and exalted, is with the congregation. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ibn Jurayj except Safwan ibn Hubayra."
"4597","Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yazid, keeper of the litters, informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take as a target anything in which there is a soul. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Hasan except Mubarak."
"4598","Muhammad ibn Salih ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: Abu Uthman al-Ubulli informed us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route; we do not know anyone narrated it from Mubarak except Uthman, without naming him."
"4599","Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Isma'il al-Judani Abd Allah ibn Isma'il informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: You and your wealth belong to your father. And this hadith was narrated by others than Abu Isma'il from Jarir, from al-Hasan, disconnected; we do not know anyone raised it with a chain except Abu Isma'il."
"4600","And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, he said: Surayj ibn al-Nu'man informed us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you come to Friday, draw near the imam, listen to the sermon, and do not engage in idle talk. And this hadith was narrated by Hisham from Qatada, from a man, from Samura."
"4601","Umar ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: My father informed me, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Matar, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The boy is pledged for his aqiqa; remove harm from him and shave his head. Qatada narrated this hadith from al-Hasan, from Samura, with wording close to this; we do not know anyone narrated it from Matar except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"4602","Khalid ibn Muhammad ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Matar, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans before they reach the market, and forbade a townsman selling for a Bedouin. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Matar, nor from Matar except Hisham."
"4603","Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Ash'ath, meaning Ibn Abd al-Malik, informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the dawn prayer is under the protection of Allah. And this hadith was narrated by Qatada and Dawud from al-Hasan, from Jundub; that is the correct in our view."
"4604","Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal informed us, from Yazid ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us in a sermon but he commanded us with charity and forbade us mutilation. Abu Bakr said: This hadith was narrated by a group from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn; the correct is from Imran ibn Husayn."
"4605","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fever is a portion of punishment, and he mentioned a phrase to that effect, so extinguish it from yourselves with cold water. He said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had fever, he would call for a skin of water and pour it over his head and bathe. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except through this route. Isma'il ibn Muslim is not strong; al-A'mash, al-Thawri, Sharik and others narrated from him."
"4606","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede the imam in bowing, for you catch up with him in what he preceded you in."
"4607","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes on Friday, let him move to the place of his companion, and let his companion move to his place. It was said to Isma'il: While the imam is preaching? He said: Yes."
"4608","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah informed us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muslim informed us, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not intentionally time your prayer to sunrise or sunset, for it rises between the two horns of Satan and sets between the two horns of Satan. Abu Bakr said: The hadiths of Isma'il ibn Muslim, we do not know anyone narrated them from al-Hasan except him."
"4609","Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar informed us, he said: Sa'id ibn Bashir informed us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Samura, may Allah be pleased with him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The severest regrets of the children of Adam in this world are three: a man with irrigated land and a water camel with which he waters his land; when it grew strong and produced its fruit, his water camel died, so he feels regret over his water camel which he knows he will not find the like of, and feels regret over the fruit of his land lest it spoil before he contrives a scheme. A man with a swift horse who met a host of disbelievers; when they drew near one another, the enemies of Allah fled, so the man outran on his horse; he does not find the like of it, and feels regret over the victory he missed which he had been on the verge of. A man with a wife whose appearance and religion pleased him, who gave birth to a boy and died in her childbirth; he feels regret over his wife, thinking he will never meet her like, and feels regret over his child, fearing its neglect before he finds one to nurse it. These are the greatest of those regrets."
"4610","And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us, he said: My father Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to me, he said: Ja'far ibn Sa'd ibn Samura informed us, he said: Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father Sulayman ibn Samura, from Samura ibn Jundub, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with similar wording. Abu Bakr said: We do not know these words narrated except from Samura, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4611","And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to me, he said: Ja'far ibn Sa'd ibn Samura informed us, he said: Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father Sulayman ibn Samura, from Samura ibn Jundub, that he wrote to his sons: From Samura ibn Jundub, peace be upon you; I praise to you Allah, besides whom there is no god. To proceed: I enjoin upon you fear of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, avoiding filth, and obeying Allah, His Messenger, and the caliphs who uphold the command of Allah. Know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to pray at night, or that one of us pray after the prescribed prayer, little or much, and make it witr."
"4612","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to pray at any hour we wished of night or day, except that he commanded us to avoid sunrise and sunset, and said: Satan disappears when it sets and rises with it."
"4613","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to guard all the prayers, and commanded us with the middle prayer, and said: It is the Asr prayer."
"4614","And with his chain, he said: He forbade us to fast continuously in the month of fasting, and it is not a binding command."
"4615","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that we greet one another when we meet."
"4616","And with his chain, he said: He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us to curse one another with the curse of Allah and His anger, and forbade us to curse one another with the Fire."
"4617","And with his chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to revile, and said: If one of you reviles his companion, let him not transgress against him, nor revile his parents, nor revile his people; but if he knows that, let him say: You are arrogant, or let him say: You are a coward, or let him say: You are a liar, or let him say: You are mean."
"4618","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to recite the Qur'an as we were taught it, and said: It was sent down upon three letters, so do not differ over it nor turn away from it, for all of it is blessed; recite it as you were taught it."
"4619","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when one of us slept through prayer or forgot it until its time in which it is prayed passes, to pray it together with the next prescribed prayer."
"4620","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when we caught the prayer while we were three, that one of us lead us."
"4621","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you establish the prayer, do not precede your reciter in bowing and prostration; rather he precedes you. When it is time for salam, send salam upon the prophets, then send salam upon your reciter and upon yourselves."
"4622","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command them, when they were in prayer, not to crouch hastily on the tips of the feet, and would say: When one of you spits in prayer, let him not spit in front of his face nor to his right, but beneath his foot, then rub it with the ground."
"4623","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When two men trade, each of them has the choice until he parts from his companion, so each chooses his desire of the sale."
"4624","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid women to lie with one another except with garments or a garment between them, and a man not to lie with his companion except with a garment between them."
"4625","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid a Muslim to draw a weapon against a Muslim."
"4626","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"4627","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Whichever of you makes food enough for two men, it suffices three; or makes food enough for four, it suffices five."
"4628","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to build mosques in our quarters, and clean and purify them, Allah willing."
"4629","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us to attend Friday and not be absent from it, and said: Each of you is more entitled to his seat when he returns to it."
"4630","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: When one of you dozes on Friday, let him move from his seat to another place."
"4631","And with his chain: that a Bedouin man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his ruling on what is forbidden to him and what is lawful for him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Lawful to you are the good things, and forbidden to you are the filthy things, except that you are compelled to food not lawful to you, so you eat of it until you are sufficed."
"4632","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us not to take out charity from slaves."
"4633","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little."
"4634","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: When one of you prays, let him say: O Allah, distance between me and my sin as You distanced between the east and the west; O Allah, I seek refuge in You lest You turn Your face from me on the Day of Resurrection; O Allah, cleanse me of sins as the white garment is cleansed of filth; O Allah, keep me alive as a Muslim and cause me to die as a Muslim."
"4635","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: Each of you is about to wish to look at me a single look, dearer to him than his wealth."
"4636","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: You are about to be among people like salt in food; food is not sound except with salt."
"4637","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is not a man of you but I hold his waistband lest he fall into the Fire."
"4638","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid plunder."
"4639","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: The Hour will not come until the stone points to the Jew, saying: O servant of Allah, this, I think he said, behind me is a Jew."
"4640","And with his chain: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The False Messiah, the Dajjal, is blind in the left eye, over it a thick growth; he heals the blind-born, gives life to the dead, and says: I am your lord. Whoever holds fast to Allah and says: My Lord is Allah, until he dies, there is no punishment upon him; whoever says: You are my lord, is tempted."
"4641","4635 - With the same chain that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The False Messiah, the Dajjal, when he emerges will remain on earth as long as Allah wills, then Jesus son of Mary (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will come from the east, affirming Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and following his religion, then he will kill the Dajjal. And it is only after that that the Hour will be established, and before the Hour comes you will see great events about which you will say: were we ever told of these? When you see that, remember Allah and know that these are the beginnings of the Hour."""
"4642","4636 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It is not lawful for a Muslim man to mutilate his slave nor to castrate him; whoever does that to him, the like of it will be done to him."""
"4643","4637 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated to me, from his father Sulayman ibn Samura, from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command hospitality for the guest, and he forbade us to milk a man's livestock without his permission, and he said: ""Their milk is like what is in your bowls"" - or a phrase like it - ""neither of them is more lawful than the other."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4644","4638 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""The sun and the moon are not eclipsed for the death of any one of you, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah by which He seeks repentance from His servants, to see who fears Him and who remembers Him. When you see that, hasten to the remembrance of Allah and remember Him."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain, and this wording is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route."
"4645","4639 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""Do not go out to meet the incoming caravans before they reach their market, and do not sell on behalf of the Bedouins even if he is the brother or father or mother of one of you."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4646","4640 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sells land or a house, the neighbor of the house or the land has most right to it."""
"4647","4641 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""When two men both marry a woman, the more deserving of the two husbands is the first of them; and in a sale, when two men buy one commodity, the more deserving of them is the first of them."""
"4648","4642 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid shighar marriage between women."
"4649","4643 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid that when there are three people, two of them whisper privately excluding the third. This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4650","4644 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us when we went on campaign that if a man called out at the rear of the people saying ""O first one,"" we should wait for him until he catches up. This hadith, we do not recall its wording except from Samura from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this chain."
"4651","4645 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command the Emigrants to advance and to be in the front rows, and he said: ""They know prayer better than the foolish and the Bedouins, and I do not like the Bedouins to be in front of them while they do not know how prayer is."" These words, we do not know anyone narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except Samura with this chain."
"4652","4646 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid that when a man is invited to food, he brings someone else along with him unless the hosts permit him. These words, we do not know them narrated except from Samura with this chain."
"4653","4647 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In Paradise there is a tree standing alone on a single trunk, the width of its trunk is seventy-two years (of travel)."" These words, we do not know them narrated with this wording except from Samura with this chain."
"4654","4648 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""The name of the man is al-karm (the vine, the noble) because of what Allah has honored him with above creation; you call grapes (al-inab), but its name is al-jawhar; it is the man, and he is al-karm."" These words, their meaning has been narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), but as for the wording of the hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Samura with this chain."
"4655","4649 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""Al-Firdaws is the hill of Paradise, the middle of it, which is its highest and best."""
"4656","4650 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""A man's soul is never filled with wealth until it is filled with dust; if one of you had a valley full from its top to its bottom, he would love to have another valley filled for him, and if the other valley were filled and he went and found another valley, he would say: By Allah, if I could I would fill you."" These words, we do not know them narrated from Samura except with this chain, though something like its meaning with different wording has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through other routes."
"4657","4651 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""I find among animals: an animal better than a hundred, and among men: a man better than a hundred men."" These words, we do not know them narrated with this wording except from Samura with this chain, though something like its meaning has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4658","4652 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went on campaign or traveled and then came back returning to Madinah, used to say: ""Returning, praising, worshipping our Lord."" These words, we do not know them narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4659","4653 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them, on the day he came to the rocky dwellings of Thamud, from a well beside the town, that anyone drink from it or draw water, and he forbade us to enter their houses."
"4660","4654 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Beware of extremism! For many of the Children of Israel went to extremes, until a short woman would make wooden sandals and stuff them, then put her feet into them, then stand beside a tall woman and walk with her, so that she appeared equal to her or taller than her."" These words, we do not know them narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4661","4655 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sought rain, used to say: ""O Allah, place in our land its adornment; O Allah, place in our land its habitation."""
"4662","4656 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them on the day of the Conquest: ""This year is the Greater Hajj; the hajj of the Muslims and the hajj of the polytheists have coincided in three consecutive days, and the hajj of the Christians and the Jews have coincided in six consecutive days. They have not coincided since the heavens and earth were created, nor will they coincide after this year until the Hour comes."" These words, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from Samura with this chain."
"4663","4657 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, he said: Jafar ibn Sad ibn Samura narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Sulayman ibn Samura narrated to me, from his father Sulayman ibn Samura, from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Ghifar - may Allah forgive it; and Aslam - may Allah grant it peace."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4664","4658 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Do not swear by idols (al-tawaghi) nor swear by your fathers; swear by Allah."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4665","4659 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""The Arabs are the sons of Sam son of Noah, the Romans are the sons of Japheth son of Noah, and the Abyssinians are the sons of Ham son of Noah."""
"4666","4660 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""When the polytheists fight you, kill their old men and spare their youth."""
"4667","4661 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Two months do not complete sixty nights."" The meaning of this hadith is what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The two months of Eid do not decrease: Ramadan and Dhul-Hijjah"" - he said: they are not fifty-eight."
"4668","4662 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he cursed the polytheists in prayer, would begin with Quraysh, then follow them with many other Arab tribes. It was said to him: Curse the disbelievers of Quraysh, so when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to curse he would say: ""O Allah, curse the disbelievers of the sons of so-and-so."" These words, we do not know anyone narrated them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Samura."
"4669","4663 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""It was said to me: Recite to Umar ibn al-Khattab, so he called him and commanded him to attend the Quran when it was revealed so he could recite it to him."" These words, we do not know them narrated except from Samura with this chain."
"4670","4664 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek forgiveness for the believing men and believing women and the Muslim men and Muslim women every Friday. These words, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from Samura with this chain."
"4671","4665 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""Abu Bakr interprets dreams, and the righteous dream is a portion of prophethood."" We do not know these words narrated except from Samura with this chain."
"4672","4666 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""Whoever kills a slain man, his spoils belong to him."" We do not know these words narrated from Samura except with these words."
"4673","4667 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""Whoever of you is killed patiently, killed in the path of Allah, he is in Paradise."" These words, we do not know them narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4674","4668 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""There is no envy in this world except in two: a man envies a man that he is given much wealth and spends from it abundantly, so the other says: If I had wealth like this one I would spend as he spends, and I would spend it in what he spends it in, so he envies him; and a man whom Allah has taught the Quran - I think he said - and he stands with it, so he says: If Allah had taught me like this I would stand as he stands."" We do not know these words narrated from Samura except with this chain."
"4675","4669 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The example of the woman is like the rib: if one wants to straighten the rib he cannot straighten it without breaking it, and it is crooked."""
"4676","4670 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""You will be gathered to Bayt al-Maqdis, then you will assemble on the Day of Resurrection."""
"4677","4671 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the battle-cry of the Emigrants ""O Banu Abd al-Rahman,"" and the battle-cry of the Khazraj ""O Banu Abd Allah,"" and the battle-cry of the Aws ""O Banu Ubayd Allah."""
"4678","4672 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""Seventy thousand of this nation will enter Paradise without reckoning"" - I think he said: ""of this nation."""
"4679","4673 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to command us, when we were frightened, to hold to unity, patience, and calm, and when we fought."
"4680","4674 - Khalid ibn Yusuf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Khubayb ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from his father Sulayman ibn Samura, from Samura ibn Jundub (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid the owner of palm trees to take on debt against the fruit of his palms until some of its fruit was eaten, fearing he would take on much debt and then the fruit would spoil; and he used to forbid the owner of crops to take on debt against his crop until it reached harvest."
"4681","4675 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say to us: ""By Allah, it would not please me to have Uhud all in gold."""
"4682","4676 - With the same chain that a man came to the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him about eating the dabb lizard, and he said: ""I neither command it nor forbid it."""
"4683","4677 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us the domestic donkey, and commanded us to throw away what we had of it, so we threw it away."
"4684","4678 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you dies he has three friends: among them one who withholds from him what he asks, and that is his wealth; and among them a friend who goes with him until he enters the grave, giving him nothing and withholding nothing, and those are his relatives; and among them a friend who says: I am with you, I go with you wherever you go and will never leave you, and that is his deeds, whether good or evil."""
"4685","4679 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid a man to cut a thong between his fingers, or he used to forbid one of us that a thong be cut between his fingers."
"4686","4680 - With the same chain that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: ""When a man makes a claim against another and one of them calls his companion to the one who judges between them and he refuses to come, he has no right."""
"4687","4682 - With the same chain from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when it rained upon us on a journey and the call to prayer was made, he would command the caller to announce: ""Pray in your saddles,"" lest it be hard upon us. End of the Musnad of Samura, which is the end of the thirty-seventh, and praise be to Allah abundantly as He deserves, then blessings upon Muhammad His Prophet and His servant."
"4688","4682 - Musnad of Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). What Jabir ibn Abd Allah narrated from Ibn Abbas: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir from Ibn Abbas."
"4689","4683 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: my grandfather Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""All who pledged allegiance under the tree will enter Paradise except the owner of the red camel."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it saying ""from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas"" except Azhar from al-Taymi from Khidash, and we do not know anyone who corroborated him in it; and Jabir did not narrate from Ibn Abbas except two hadiths, both with this chain, both narrated by Azhar."
"4690","4684 - And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Azhar narrated to us from Sulayman al-Taymi from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas."
"4691","4685 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: my grandfather Azhar ibn Sad narrated to me from Sulayman al-Taymi from Khidash, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When one of you lies on his back, let him not place one of his feet upon the other."" This hadith was narrated by more than one from Jabir from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and none said ""from Jabir, from Ibn Abbas"" except Azhar from al-Taymi from Khidash; and Khidash, we do not know anyone narrated from him except al-Taymi and Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Asri, and Khidash is Basran."
"4692","4686 - Anas from Ibn Abbas: Bishr ibn Adam and Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us from Qatada, from Anas, that some Zut people were brought to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and he wanted to burn them, so Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever changes his religion, kill him."" This hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it except Abd al-Samad, and Anas narrated from Ibn Abbas nothing but this hadith."
"4693","4687 - Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Abbas: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Fitr narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: Your people claim that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran (ramal) and that it is a sunnah. He said: They lied and they told the truth: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did run, but it is not a sunnah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while the polytheists were on the mountain of Quayqian, and it reached him that they were saying that the Messenger of Allah and his Companions were weakened, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran and commanded his Companions to run so the polytheists would see that they had strength."
"4694","4688 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4695","4689 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Ala informed us, he said: al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Fitr from Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Abbas about the coming of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Makkah. This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through various routes, and narrated from Abu al-Tufayl from Ibn Abbas through more than one route; those we mentioned suffice, unless someone other than those we mentioned adds some wording, in which case it is written for the sake of the addition."
"4696","4690 - Bishr ibn Muadh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym narrated to us from Said ibn Jubayr and Abu al-Tufayl, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Makkah and said: ""You are the most beloved of Allah's land to Allah; had your people not expelled me from you, I would not have left."" This hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayra and others, and we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas with a chain better than this chain; some who narrated it from Ibn Khuthaym said: from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas, without mentioning Abu al-Tufayl, while Bishr combined both from Fudayl."
"4697","4691 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us from Ibn Khuthaym, from Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only touched the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner. Muawiya said: Nothing of the House is to be left untouched, and he touched all the corners. This hadith, something like its wording has been narrated from other than Ibn Abbas, and it has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through other than this route; and this chain is the best chain narrated on that from Ibn Abbas."
"4698","4692 - Said ibn al-Musayyib from Ibn Abbas: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4699","4693 - And Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Said ibn Abi Aruba from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4700","4694 - Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us from Muhammad ibn Ali from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4701","4694 (m) - And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us from Umar ibn al-Harith from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like the one who returns to his vomit."" This hadith has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through various routes, and these chains are the best and most eminent chains narrated from Said ibn al-Musayyib from Ibn Abbas; and the most eminent who narrated this hadith from Ibn Abbas is Said ibn al-Musayyib."
"4702","4695 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman Abu al-Jumahir narrated to us, he said: Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us from Qatada, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever parts from the community the measure of a span has removed the yoke of Islam from his neck; whoever dies with no imam over him, his death is a death of ignorance; and whoever dies under a blind banner calling to partisanship or aiding partisanship, his killing is a killing of ignorance."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Ibn Abbas with this route with this chain, and we do not know anyone narrated this hadith except Khulayd ibn Dalaj; and Khulayd is a well-known man from whom al-Walid ibn Muslim and Abu al-Jumahir and al-Nufayli and others narrated."
"4703","4696 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman, from Abu Sad, from Muawiya ibn Ishaq, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever walks to his debtor for his right, the beasts of the earth and the fish of the water pray for him, and for every step a tree is planted for him in Paradise and a sin is forgiven."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Abbas, and we do not know for it any route other than this route."
"4704","4697 - Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Qatada narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we are people of Rabia, and between us and you are the disbelievers of Mudar, and we cannot reach you except in a sacred month, so command us with a matter that if we do it we will enter Paradise and we will call to it those behind us. So he commanded them and forbade them four things: to worship Allah not associating anything with Him, to establish prayer, to give zakat, to fast Ramadan, to perform hajj to the House, and to give the fifth of the spoils; and he forbade them green jars, gourds, varnished vessels, and hollowed stumps. They said: In what shall we drink? He said: ""Drink from that whose mouths are tied shut."" This hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada from Said ibn al-Musayyib and Ikrima from Ibn Abbas except Aban ibn Yazid."
"4705","4698 - Tawus from Ibn Abbas: Abu Kamil al-Fudayl ibn al-Husayn al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Warith, meaning Ibn Said, narrated to us, from Ayyub from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4706","4699 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""Whoever buys food, let him not sell it until he takes possession of it."" This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Tawus, and a group narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, so we sufficed with those we named apart from others."
"4707","4700 - And al-Mundhir ibn al-Walid al-Jarudi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar from Ayyub from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4708","4701 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Amr from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4709","4702 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4710","4703 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us from Amr from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""I was commanded to prostrate on seven, and not to gather hair nor garment."" This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) through various routes with different wordings, and narrated from Ibn Abbas through more than one route; and a group narrated it from Amr from Tawus, so we sufficed with those we mentioned and deemed them enough apart from others."
"4711","4704 - Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: my father Abd al-Warith narrated to us from Ayyub from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not forbid renting out land, but he said: ""For a man to lend his brother his land is better for him than to take rent for it."""
"4712","4705 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. This hadith has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) similarly through various routes, and this is among the best chains narrated on that."
"4713","4706 - And Ahmad ibn Abda and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Ata and Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had himself cupped while in ihram. The wording in this hadith is the wording of Amr ibn Ali. This hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Amr from Tawus except Ibn Uyayna; and it has been narrated from Ibn Abbas through other than this route, and from other than Ibn Abbas as well."
"4714","4707 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyayna narrated to us from Amr from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling fruits until they are edible. This hadith was narrated by others than Ubayd Allah, from Ibn Uyayna from Amr from Tawus, mursal."
"4715","4708 - And Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghufra al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Every condition not in the Book of Allah is void, even if a hundred conditions."""
"4716","4709 - And Ahmad ibn Abda narrated it to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Amr from Tawus, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not mention Ibn Abbas. We do not know anyone who corroborated Amr ibn Yahya in his narration from Amr from Tawus from Ibn Abbas. And these words are narrated from other than Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4717","4710 - And Hawthara ibn Muhammad al-Minqari narrated to us from his book, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""All of Arafah is a standing place, and all of Mina is a slaughter place."""
"4718","4711 - And Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us from Amr from Tawus, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly, and he did not say from Ibn Abbas. This hadith, we do not know anyone who said ""from Tawus from Ibn Abbas"" except Hawthara, and we do not know anyone who corroborated him in it; and the hadith is famous from Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated through various routes, except that it is not narrated from Amr from Tawus except through this route."
"4719","4712 - Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a Bedouin gave a gift to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave him something and said to him: ""Are you pleased?"" He said: No. Then he increased him and said: ""Are you pleased?"" He said: No. Then he increased him and said: ""Are you pleased?"" He said: Yes. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I had intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi, or an Ansari, or a Thaqafi."" This hadith, we do not know anyone who said ""from Tawus from Ibn Abbas"" except Yunus ibn Muhammad from Hammad ibn Zayd; and Ibn Uyayna narrated it."
"4720","4713 - Ahmad ibn Abda narrated it to us from Ibn Uyayna from Amr from Tawus, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). We do not know these words narrated from Ibn Abbas except through this route, and we do not recall anyone narrated it from Yunus from Hammad except Ibrahim ibn Said; then some of our companions mentioned that Mujahid ibn Musa also narrated it from Yunus, thus corroborating Ibrahim in its chain."
"4721","4714 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, marfu, he said: ""Whoever is killed in blind partisanship - or he said: blind partisanship - with a stone or a whip or a stick, upon him is the blood-money of mistake; and whoever is killed deliberately, it is retaliation; and whoever stands between him and it, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people; neither repentance nor ransom will be accepted from him."" This hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Abbas with this wording except through this route with this chain; and we do not know anyone who raised it from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from Ibn Abbas except Sulayman ibn Kathir, while others than Sulayman narrated it from Amr ibn Dinar from Tawus from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), mursal."
"4722","4715 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, he said: I heard Ikrima say - and I do not think him but from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) - the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one who takes back his gift is like the dog returning to its vomit."""
"4723","4716 - Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: I heard Layth narrating from Abu Fazara from Said ibn Jubayr, or Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""These words are a protection from every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and all His names in general from the evil of the poisonous and the common, and from the evil of the piercing eye, and from the evil of the envier when he envies, and from the evil of the possessor of evil and what he begets. Thirty-three of the angels came with them, and he said: affliction and affliction. He said: Take dust from your land and wipe your forelocks; and in it: whoever takes a fetter upon it, or conceals it from anyone, will never prosper then ever."""
"4724","4717 - And Ismail ibn Sayf al-Qutai narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Arqam narrated to us, he said: al-Amash narrated to us from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas that Ali (may Allah be pleased with them) handed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dust, and he threw it in the faces of the polytheists on the day of Hunayn."
"4725","4718 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Kirmani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Idris ibn bint Wahb ibn Munabbih from Wahb, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked Gabriel to see him in his form. He said: Call upon your Lord. So he called upon his Lord, and he rose upon him from the east, rising and moving; when he saw him he fell unconscious, and he came to him."
"4726","4719 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Husayn ibn Abd Allah, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when the sun had passed its zenith while he was at home, would combine Zuhr and Asr; and if it had not passed its zenith until he departed, he would travel until when it was Asr he would dismount and combine Zuhr and Asr; and when the sun had set for him he would combine Maghrib and Isha at home; and if he departed before it set, he would travel until when the twilight had set he would dismount and combine Maghrib and Isha."
"4727","4720 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Umayya narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Ibn Abbas - and others said: from Abu al-Zubayr from Said ibn Jubayr from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When your brothers were struck, Allah placed their souls in the bellies of green birds that visit the rivers of Paradise and eat of its fruits and shelter in lamps hung in the shade of the Throne. When they found the goodness of their food and drink, they said: If only they knew of what honor we have. Allah, blessed and exalted, said: I will inform them of you. So Allah revealed: {And never think of those who have been killed in the cause of Allah as dead. Rather, they are alive with their Lord, receiving provision, rejoicing in what Allah has bestowed upon them of His bounty, and they receive good tidings about those who have not yet joined them from behind them, that there will be no fear concerning them, nor will they grieve}."""
"4728","4721 - Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us from Dawud, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Saba wind came to the North wind and said: Go so we may aid the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The North wind said: The free woman does not travel by night. So the wind by which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was aided was the Saba."
"4729","4722 - And Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abu Khalid narrated to us from al-Amash from al-Hakam and Muslim al-Batin from Said ibn Jubayr and Ata and Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My sister died with two consecutive months of fasting due upon her. He said: ""Tell me, if your sister had a debt, would you pay it?"" She said: Yes. He said: ""Then the right of Allah is more deserving."""
"4730","4723 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: my father informed us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us from Yala ibn Hakim from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the nabidh of jars."
"4731","4724 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me from Sufyan, from his father, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas: {While you are samidun} - he said: singing."
"4732","4725 - Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Mujalid narrated to us from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The example of one who speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like the example of the donkey carrying books."""
"4733","4726 - Ismail ibn Abd Allah al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Khattab ibn Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughira narrated to us from his father from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to walk among the palm trees in Madinah, and people began saying: In it is a sa, and in it is a wasq. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""In it is such and such."" They said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. So the Messenger of Allah said: ""I am only a human; what I narrate to you from Allah is truth, and what I say from myself, I am only a human who is right and who errs."""
"4734","4727 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muadh ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me from Qatada, from Abu Qilaba from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj from Abd Allah ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw my Lord in the best form, and He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and blessed. He said: About what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: My Lord, I do not know. He said: So He placed His hand between my shoulders and I felt its coolness between my breasts, and I knew what is between the east and the west. He said: O Muhammad. I said: At Your service, my Lord, and blessed. He said: About what does the highest assembly dispute? I said: My Lord, about expiations, and walking on feet to the congregations, and completing ablution in disliked circumstances, and waiting for prayer after prayer until the prayers. Whoever guards them lives well, dies well, and is of his sins as on the day he was born."""
"4735","4728 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, and from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us the tashahhud as he taught us the Quran. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Greetings, blessed praises, prayers, good words to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger."""
"4736","4729 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shaddad ibn Said narrated to us from al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadra, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O youth of Quraysh, do not commit adultery; guard your private parts. Indeed, whoever guards his private part, for him is Paradise."""
"4737","4730 - Abu Farwa Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: my father Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Ruhawi narrated to us from his father Yazid ibn Sinan, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he placed me on his right."
"4738","4731 - He said: And my father Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to me from his father Yazid ibn Sinan, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Dubaa: ""Enter ihram and say the talbiya and say: My place of release is on earth where You confine me; for if you fall ill, you have become released by the command of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."""
"4739","4732 - He said: And my father narrated to me from his father Yazid, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform hajj after migrating except one hajj, and it is that hajj in which he began with umra before hajj. Abd Allah ibn al-Abbas said: So did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he put an umra before hajj. Abd Allah said: Umra does not detract anything from hajj, nor does hajj detract anything from umra, and that is good and that is truth; but Satan confuses you."
"4740","4733 - He said: And my father narrated to me from his father, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Aisha to perform umra from al-Tanim, then to circumambulate the House, though she had not circumambulated because of her menstruation, and she had entered ihram for umra."
"4741","4734 - He said: And my father narrated to me from his father, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I would never perform hajj except that I sacrifice; so did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4742","4735 - He said: And my father narrated to me from his father, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Whoever circumambulates between al-Safa and al-Marwa, putting it forward for his umra, that suffices him for his umra and his hajj; and so did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his departure: he circumambulated for his umra, then remained, then departed from hajj and did not circumambulate after hajj until he departed."
"4743","4736 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us from Qatada, from Abu Talib al-Dubai."
"4744","4737 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith informed us, he said: Said narrated to us from Qatada, from Abu Talib al-Dubai, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a cupper called Abu Tayba cupped the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he gave him his wage and reduced for him some of his labor, or remitted part of his labor."
"4745","4738 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us from Ibn Jurayj from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Allah's anger intensified against one whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) killed with his hand, and Allah's anger intensified against a people who bloodied the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4746","4739 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Abu Raja, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The affair of this nation will remain sound, or near to it - Jarir said: or a word like it - so long as they do not speak about predestination and children."""
"4747","4740 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Said narrated to us from Qatada, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he used to combine the two prayers on a journey and say: It is of the sunnah."
"4748","4741 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: ""The black dog and the menstruating woman cut off prayer."" He said: I said: He used to mention a third. He said: What is it? I said: The donkey. He said: Gently, the donkey. I said: He mentioned a fourth. He said: What is it? I said: The disbeliever. He said: If you can, let neither a disbeliever nor a Muslim pass in front of you, do so."
"4749","4742 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Said from Qatada, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, like the hadith of Shuba, and he did not raise it."
"4750","4743 - Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Muhammad Abu Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Hasan al-Thalabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Yala al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abu Sad, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, is a town destroyed while the righteous are in it? He said: Yes. It was said: How? He said: ""By their flattery and their silence about disobedience to Allah."""
"4751","4744 - And Abu Shayba narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayda narrated to us from al-Amash from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A barren wind seized them on the day of Badr."
"4752","4745 - Abd Allah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Sawada narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us from Zadham, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever performs hajj on foot, for every step seven hundred good deeds of the good deeds of the Sanctuary are written for him."" Some said: And what are the good deeds of the Sanctuary? He said: ""Every good deed is a hundred thousand good deeds."""
"4753","4746 - And Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: I bear witness that I knew the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over the two leather socks."
"4754","4747 - Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn Mamul narrated to us, he said: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Umara narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Asbahani, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A freed slave of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell from a palm tree and died, so the Prophet gave his inheritance to the people of his religion."
"4755","4748 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Yala narrated to us from al-Hakam from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Two slave girls came out walking in front of the qibla while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, so he took them by their waists; when he wanted to bow he separated between them, then bowed."
"4756","4749 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us from al-Minhal ibn Amr from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: My mother owes a slave to free, and I have a black slave girl. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Bring her to me."" The Messenger of Allah said to her: ""Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" She said: Yes. He said: ""Then free her."""
"4757","4750 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us from Abd al-Karim, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), about one who has intercourse with his wife while she is menstruating: if the blood is fresh, let him give a dinar in charity, and if it is yellowish, half a dinar."
"4758","4751 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us from Sharik from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) poured forth from Jam, or Arafah, with Qutham before him and al-Fadl behind him."
"4759","4752 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Jabir, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) legislated two rakahs on a journey, and they are complete, and witr on a journey is sunnah."
"4760","4753 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr in Madinah without fear or rain. I said to Ibn Abbas: Why did he do that? He said: So as not to burden his nation."
"4761","4754 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr and Asr and Maghrib and Isha while resident in Madinah without fear, so as not to burden his nation."
"4762","4755 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a campaign would delay Zuhr until it cooled, then pray Zuhr and Asr, then not dismount until the twilight set, then pray Maghrib and Isha."
"4763","4756 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Sufyan from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Some Ansar people passed by me shooting at a dove, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade taking a living soul as a target."
"4764","4757 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Ala from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever speaks about the Quran without knowledge, let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"4765","4758 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Abu Awana narrated to us from Abd al-Ala from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever lies upon me deliberately - or said: upon me what I did not say - let him take his seat in the Fire."""
"4766","4759 - Al-Qasim ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Atiyya narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr in the first rakah: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, in the second: {Say: O disbelievers}, and in the third: {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"4767","4760 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray witr with: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Say: O disbelievers}, and {Say: He is Allah, the One}."
"4768","4761 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Israil, from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: He was asked: How old were you when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away? He said: I was then circumcised."
"4769","4762 - Al-Husayn ibn Alawayh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from his father from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was born in the Year of the Elephant."
"4770","4763 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Atiyya narrated to us, he said: ... narrated to us from Abu Ishaq, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""There are no days in which deeds are better than these days,"" meaning the ten days. It was said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: ""Not even jihad in the path of Allah."""
"4771","4764 - Usayd ibn Asim narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Yaqub al-Qummi narrated to us from Jafar ibn Abi al-Mughira from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us while a cloud had shaded us and we were hopeful of it, and he said: ""The angel who drives it, or drives this cloud, came to me and greeted me, and informed me that he drives it to such-and-such valley."""
"4772","4765 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Amr ibn Malik al-Nukri narrated to us from his father, from Abu al-Jawza, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished his prayer he would say: ""There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise; in His hand is good, and He is over all things capable. O Allah, none withholds what You give, and none gives what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate avails him nothing against You."""
"4773","4766 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Israil narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled a fifth for buried treasure."
"4774","4767 - With his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The righteous dream is a part of seventy parts of prophethood."""
"4775","4768 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""A man should not touch a man, nor a woman a woman."""
"4776","4769 - With his chain he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, when he had finished Badr: Go for the caravan, there is nothing before it. Al-Abbas called to him while he was a captive in bonds: It is not right for you. He said: Why? He said: For Allah promised you one of the two parties, and He has given you what He promised you."
"4777","4770 - With his chain he said: They said: O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while drinking wine? Then was revealed: {There is not upon those who believe and do righteous deeds any blame concerning what they tasted}."
"4778","4771 - With his chain he said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what about those who died while praying toward Bayt al-Maqdis? So Allah, blessed and exalted, revealed: {And Allah would never cause your faith to be lost}. Ubayd Allah said: This is between prayer being of faith."
"4779","4772 - With his chain he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""No contagion, no Safar, no omen, no hama."" A man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man takes a mangy sheep and throws it among a hundred sheep and it makes them mangy. He said: ""Then who made the first one mangy?"""
"4780","4773 - With his chain, a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praising him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Some eloquence is magic, and some poetry is wisdom."""
"4781","4774 - With his chain he said: Maiz ibn Malik was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and confessed twice, so he said: ""Take him away."" Then he was brought back and confessed twice, until he confessed four times, so he said: ""Go and stone him."" Thus I found it in my book, from Ikrima from Ibn Abbas; but it is only from Said ibn Jubayr, the hadith of Maiz ibn Malik in particular."
"4782","4775 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Salih narrated to us from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: There were Qurayza and al-Nadir, and al-Nadir were nobler than Qurayza. If a man of Qurayza killed a man of al-Nadir, he was killed for him; and if a man of al-Nadir killed a man of Qurayza, they said: Hand him to us to kill him. They said: Between us and you is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they came to him, and was revealed: {And if you judge, judge between them with justice}, and justice is a soul for a soul. Then was revealed: {Then is it the judgement of ignorance they desire?}."
"4783","4776 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, from Salim Abu Hammad from al-Suddi, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I was given five that none of the prophets before me was given: the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, while no prophet among the prophets would pray until he reached his prayer-niche; and I was aided with terror the distance of a month, it being before me toward the polytheists, so Allah casts terror into their hearts; and a prophet would be sent to his own people particularly, while I was sent to jinn and mankind; and the prophets would set aside the fifth and fire would come and consume it, while I was commanded to distribute it among the poor of my nation; and no prophet remains but he was given intercession, while I delayed my intercession for my nation."""
"4784","4777 - Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Isam ibn Qudama narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: ""Would that I knew which of you is the owner of the much-haired camel, who will go out and the dogs of Hawab will bark at her, and many will be killed on her right and on her left, then she will escape after nearly being lost."""
"4785","4778 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Talha narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us from Simak, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: There were two co-wives between whom there was anger, so one of them threw at the other and she miscarried a dead boy whose hair had grown. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled against the liable kin. His uncle said: O Messenger of Allah, she miscarried a dead boy whose hair had grown. The father of the killer said: He lies; by Allah, he neither cried nor ate nor drank, so the like of him is to be void. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The rhymed speech of ignorance and its soothsaying? In the child is a ghurra."" He said: The name of one of them was Mulayka and the other Umm Atruf."
"4786","Umar ibn al-Khattab and Sahl ibn Bahr both narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Hammad ibn Talhah al-Qannad narrated to us, he said: Asbat ibn Nasr narrated to us, from Simak, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: A mouse came and began dragging the wick. He said: The servant girl went to drive it away, so the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave it. He said: So it brought it and threw it in front of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) onto the mat he was sitting on, and it burned an area of it about the size of a dirham. Then he said: When you sleep, extinguish your lamps, for Satan directs this (creature) to this, and so it burns you."
"4787","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: Twenty men from among the freed slaves were present at Badr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"4788","Sahl narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from al-Nahwi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: One thousand men from Banu Sulaym were present with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah."
"4789","Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ismah narrated to us, from Abu al-Sabbah, from Abu Hashim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are three upon whom there is no reckoning for what they eat, if Allah wills, so long as it is lawful: the fasting person, the one eating sahur, and the one stationed on guard in the path of Allah."
"4790","Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dispatched Ibn Maslamah and his companions to Ibn al-Ashraf to kill him, he walked with them to Baqi al-Gharqad, then sent them off and said: Go forth in the name of Allah. O Allah, aid them."
"4791","Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Zakariyya, the freed slave of Banu Asad, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Awn al-Khurasani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no one but that he will meet Allah having intended a sin or committed it, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya, for he neither intended it nor committed it."
"4792","Sahl narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated, a slave of Salam feared his family would follow the Prophet, so they shackled him. He wrote to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You know of my Islam, so send me (a mount) or rescue me. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent seven men on one camel and said: Perhaps you will find in his house someone to help you against him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed him."
"4793","Uqbah ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj ibn Artah informed me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that he did not consider it necessary to stay at al-Abtah, and he would say: It is only a place where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed and pitched his tent therein."
"4794","Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An Umrah in Ramadan equals a Hajj."
"4795","Abdullah ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Hafs, meaning Ibn Ghiyath, narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a dead sheep lying on its legs and said: It would not have harmed its owners had they benefited from its hide. So Sawdah tanned it and made nabidh in it."
"4796","Muhammad ibn Muawiyah ibn Malij narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling palm trees for two or three years: that (dates) be bought while on the tops of the palms for a measured amount, or that the fruit be sold before its soundness appears."
"4797","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Hajjaj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not stone (the Jamarat) until the sun had passed its zenith."
"4798","al-Hasan ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from Sharik, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gifted one hundred sacrificial camels, garlanded and covered."
"4799","al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti al-Darir narrated to us, he said: Ishaq narrated to us, from Sharik, from Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that al-Saab ibn Jaththamah gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was in ihram, the hindquarter of a donkey, so he returned it and did not eat it."
"4800","Ubaydullah ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My uncle narrated to me, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from al-Hajjaj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away while I was, Abu al-Hasan said: I think he said, circumcised."
